{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs","id":667904,"title":"Lets design Abyssals Sigs.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-17T00:02:59-07:00","id":667904,"title":"Lets design Abyssals Sigs.","content":"so I read in the &quot;taking loyalists serious&quot; thread that the solar sigs are being changed for 3Ex. Now i wonder, since the same thing will probably happen to the other sigs. I more or less became pretty interested in how would you guys and gals design the abyssal sigs?<br /> <br /> I hope i make sense.<br /> <br /> P.S. I will probably make a quick lineart drawing of those suggestions that really &quot;speaks&quot; to me<br /> <br /> I may need to change this things title to just Lets Design Abyssals!<br /> <br /> those that have spoken to me so far are<br /> Laughing Death Dusk caste: <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/art/Laughing-Death-583555146\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/art/La...eath-583555146</a><br /> Subject seven Moonshadow caste: <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/art/Subject-Seven-581681433\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/art/Su...even-581681433</a><br /> Ten Plagues Dagger Daybreak caste created by me: <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/art/Ten-Plagues-Dagger-565133312\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/art/Te...gger-565133312</a><br /> Murder so foul Day caste created by me: <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/art/Murder-so-Foul-563750262\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/art/Mu...Foul-563750262</a><br /> She who Hunts with Darkness Day caste created by me<br /> (sorry if there where any awesome days out there and i missed them): <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/art/She-who-hunts-with-darkness-561442879\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/art/Sh...ness-561442879</a><br /> Unbound Brutality of War Dusk caste created by me<br /> (sorry if there where any awesome dusks out there and i missed them): <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/art/Unbound-Brutality-of-War-561198029\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/art/Un...-War-561198029</a><br /> Herald of Ashes Midnight caste created by Rahu444: <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/art/Herald-of-Ashes-561166257\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/art/He...shes-561166257</a><br /> the Bloody-Handed General Daybreak caste by Wastevens: <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/art/The-Bloody-Handed-General-560970940\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/art/Th...eral-560970940</a><br /> Jiangshi Moonshadow caste by the Wizard of Oz: <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/art/Jiangshi-moonshadow-caste-560795099\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/art/Ji...aste-560795099</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":4455,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","user":"Xanroth","date":". 01-10-2016, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T00:25:30-07:00","id":667945,"title":"","content":"The Jiangshi is a traditional Chinese undead creature that dresses in the robes of a Qing bureaucrat. Since Exalted is one of the few games that lets you play a Kung-fu bureaucrat, I think that would make an excellent design for a Moonshadow. <br /> <br /> At least one of them should show the hideous Abyssal form (if that's still a thing). some kind of zombie-dude (or dudette).<br /> <br /> For a Midnight, I wonder if there's something you can do with a gothic priest (not another stripper-nun though please).<br /> How do you show &quot;gothic&quot; without a gothic castle?<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, overall, I'd like more variety, to show players you can do the Abyssals with more than one look. I'm not against the skulls motif, but it needs to make some kind of sense: the Buddhist or Hindu necklaces of skulls, the Christian tortured-guy-amulet.<br /> Maybe a barbarian head-hunter with shrunken heads?<br /> It just needs to feel like some thought's been put into it, rather than &quot;just throw skulls everywhere&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tbh, a lot of the Abyssal designs are just not that interesting. The Day caste, for example. I'm sure they could come up with something better.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T00:38:58-07:00","id":667948,"title":"","content":"I think for the Daybreak - I'd like it if they went with someone who's more of an investigator type instead of undead mad scientist this time. Someone who investigates crimes in both the Living Lands and the Underworld and uses their ability to cross between them to bring justice to the living and the dead. Might be cool to have her be from the south, give her some flame pieces. The <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/ksbd-3-52/\" target=\"_blank\">Gun Witch</a> looks pretty cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T00:48:30-07:00","id":667960,"title":"","content":"How do you make them look like an investigator though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T00:56:39-07:00","id":667964,"title":"","content":"I would like to see a Bokor inspired Midnight caste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1072-theye1","name":"theye1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1072_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T00:57:17-07:00","id":667965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=667960#post667960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you make them look like an investigator though?</div> </div> </div> </div>that can be solved with a pose actually. have her left hand covered in blood be near her nose so it almost looks like she's smelling the blood but with a calm and calculating look on her face and not a batshit insane look. that can give her the investigator feel especially if she looks like the gun witch from 6 billion demons","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T01:02:28-07:00","id":667966,"title":"","content":"Magnifying glass? I mean you could draw them with a ghost while they point to a WANTED poster on a nearby wall in the background or show them crouched over a corpse and pulling a ghost from it for questioning. There's really no indication that Fallen Tears Poet is an actual poet other than his name and his description in the Abyssal book, he's some dude in a mask and robes with a giant hammer.<br /> <br /> The Midnight could, to continue the grand tradition, be a shirtless high priest that sacrifices people by ripping their hearts out to mirror what the UCS use to do, but now it's a method of corrupting the local gods to demanding actual blood sacrifices. Kinda bloody-aztec themed - loincloth, feathered cape, sacrificial knives, necklace of bloody hearts","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T01:10:49-07:00","id":667984,"title":"","content":"well for investigator, there are a few styles:<br /> <br /> 1. The Cloak Look<br /> For the cheapest, most low-tech style possible, you can always just put on a cloak and pull its hood over your head so that your face is eternally hidden in shadows while most of your body is hidden under the cloak, real popular, and mysterious and its Ringwraith recommended!<br /> <br /> 2. Wide-Brimmed Hat And Trenchcoat<br /> For those who want to be a little more elaborate and high tech, you can't go wrong with having a big cool-looking hat while wearing a long dark trenchcoat, works in both cowboy and pirate settings so all you need to do to adjust from South to West is exchanging your flame piece for a cutlass. you may have to act a little stoic to preserve your aura of mystery though.<br /> <br /> 3. Cloak and Hat<br /> If you think a trenchcoat is not period-appropriate, you can always exchange that for a cloak while keeping the hat. add in a long thin blade like a rapier or saber and suddenly you a dashing swashbuckler!<br /> <br /> 4. Tight Leather<br /> Alternatively you can ditch all the billows and mysteriousness and just wear form fitting leather for that secret agent look and for complete freedom of movement complete with boots with hidden, belts full of knives, and you can combine it with the hood style to look like an assassin, and aren't all assassins investigators in some manner? This look also comes in ninja.<br /> <br /> 5. Sedge Hat and Kimono<br /> If you really want to play up the East Asian fantasy aspect of it, you can't go wrong by taking style no. 2 and shifting it a little. add in a katana and you look like a samurai.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T01:23:12-07:00","id":667988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=667945#post667945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Jiangshi is a traditional Chinese undead creature that dresses in the robes of a Qing bureaucrat. Since Exalted is one of the few games that lets you play a Kung-fu bureaucrat, I think that would make an excellent design for a Moonshadow.<br /> <br /> At least one of them should show the hideous Abyssal form (if that's still a thing). some kind of zombie-dude (or dudette).<br /> <br /> For a Midnight, I wonder if there's something you can do with a gothic priest (not another stripper-nun though please).<br /> How do you show &quot;gothic&quot; without a gothic castle?<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, overall, I'd like more variety, to show players you can do the Abyssals with more than one look. I'm not against the skulls motif, but it needs to make some kind of sense: the Buddhist or Hindu necklaces of skulls, the Christian tortured-guy-amulet.<br /> Maybe a barbarian head-hunter with shrunken heads?<br /> It just needs to feel like some thought's been put into it, rather than &quot;just throw skulls everywhere&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tbh, a lot of the Abyssal designs are just not that interesting. The Day caste, for example. I'm sure they could come up with something better.</div> </div> </div> </div>hmmmm the Jiangshi is one that absolutely works for a moonshadow.<br /> <br /> ohohohoho i got yah covered man. you can make most abyssals work as the monsters when you design them, the tricky part is to make them seem interesting. I suggest making the day caste look like the monster. Lets have it be a she this time, She is draped in black robes that looks like living shadows that snuffs out any light it touches with a Glasgow smile (i think that's what it's called at least) give her a scythe and give her the unavoidable reaper that will get you even if you sit inside a six feet thick safe buried tucked away under the scarlet throne inside the imperial palace.<br /> otherwise you could make one that works kind of like how one of my characters does. The Silencer of Loose Tongues. warning big picture ahead<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://pre07.deviantart.net/2e6f/th/pre/i/2015/127/3/c/silencer_of_loose_tongues_by_xanroth-d8sis31.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> it's not possible to see it on this image but his thing is that he is TO LARGE to be able to sneak around and be as silent as he is. He's wrapped up like a mummy because his deathlord (one of my custom ones) can't keep himself from experimenting on everything, including his own deathknights.<br /> <br /> for the midnight, never fear Oswald the pardoner is here <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://darksouls.wdfiles.com/local--files/npcs/oswald-of-carim-large.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> he has a pretty cool look on his clothes so i personally think it works (especially since one of my characters that happens to be a midnight shares his look, i don't have a sketch of him so but he's in the comic).<br /> <br /> the skulls and stuff yeah, that's definitely something for the dusk caste. let's call him something like, Unbound Brutality of War(worst name ever wooooh).<br /> a very large a powerfully built man covered in heavy soulsteel armor, possibly with a pair of skeletal horned best heads on his shoulders that could possibly come to life as an evocation and start to bite brutality's foes. On his back there are either a banner pole (the thing that you sometimes see on samurais) or a couple of sharpened spikes. either impaled or tied to these are the heads of foes that brutality found worthy, these heads can as a evocation be awakened and start to scream at the top of their.. err.. formerly attached lungs? This is demoralizing and will make foes flee much more easily.<br /> <br /> i hope i made some sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T01:40:45-07:00","id":667994,"title":"","content":"I had a &quot;sig&quot; Midnight Caste Abyssal in my little Creation, a pestilent and vile creature, ridden with disease and festering sores. Kept hidden under cloaks, hoods and generally being a bit like an open-sore-crossed-with-Mum-Ra. He was ... vile. A true servant of the Abyss and his Deathlord, he regularly took to the Labyrinth to breed new diseases, find old ones long gone from Creation or to speak with the things that dwell there. His services were often hired out to other Deathlords.<br /> <br /> The Solar PC, who fancied himself as something of a witty farmboy-turned-Zenith, crossed paths with the Abyssal many times; even started calling him &quot;Old Puss Boy&quot;. Soon changed his mind when a plague swept through his home town whilst he was away doing Solar stuff. The disease was fast and, due to being necromantic in origin decomposed the bodies very, very quickly. Cue lots of hungry ghosts and no bodies to burn when the Solar PC returned home. He had to dispatch the ghosts of his family, his friends etc. He was not happy ... but then again don't piss off an Abyssal....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/907-jay","name":"Jay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T02:54:32-07:00","id":668038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=667945#post667945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Jiangshi is a traditional Chinese undead creature that dresses in the robes of a Qing bureaucrat. Since Exalted is one of the few games that lets you play a Kung-fu bureaucrat, I think that would make an excellent design for a Moonshadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>here you go Oz one Jiangshi moonshadow caste. I hope i haven't butchered your idea to much<br /> warning big bloody picture. will also be available as a link in the first post<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://pre07.deviantart.net/341f/th/pre/i/2015/260/8/9/jiangshi_moonshadow_caste_by_xanroth-d99vs9n.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> I decided to have the dead exorcist in there with the paper stabbed into his eye to more or less give the moonshadow a feel of that when this guy kills he adds a cruel twist to it (aka he stabbed someone to death with the very thing that is supposed to neutralize a jiangshi). I hope i made sense","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":4455,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","user":"Xanroth","date":". 09-17-2015, 06:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T03:51:41-07:00","id":668054,"title":"","content":"This time around, the Daybreak sig <i>needs</i> to be a witch doctor, inspired by voodoo, or rather the pulp version of pop culture depictions of voodoo, crossed with a healthy dose of swamp witch; <br /> I'm picturing someone talking to shrunken heads, raining poison frogs on her enemies, and on a smaller scales acting as a midwife and occasional provider of euthanasia to her community. The whole shabang included. Tiki masks. Voodoo dolls. Hexbags. Curses.<br /> Fuck yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T04:14:32-07:00","id":668061,"title":"","content":"Petition to keep Fallen Tears Poet as-is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T04:18:22-07:00","id":668063,"title":"","content":"To be fair, he is the only one I like. He's got a funerary mask, a monk-esque habit (gothically appropriate), and his skin's rotting off, so he stands out from the others. I also vaguely remember him having an interesting backstory, goals, etc, unlike the others (always a psycho, necro-surgeon, cheap whore, and I can't remember), though I don't really remember what they were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T04:25:32-07:00","id":668068,"title":"","content":"The sig Abyssals really suffered from Abyssals basically being one-note Solars and Deathlords + the Underworld being boring. <br /> <br /> Prince of Shadows had an interesting backstory too IIRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T05:15:40-07:00","id":668091,"title":"","content":"He was from Sijan, right, a gravedigger's apprentice who froze to death? But then he just looked so... stereotypical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T05:55:50-07:00","id":668118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=667960#post667960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you make them look like an investigator though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Trench-coat and fedora?<br /> <br /> As for me:<br /> <br /> Dusk - The Weapon:<br /> While I actually like the Maiden (&quot;It amused me&quot;, has always been a favourite motive), I'd move the obligatory sociopath into Daybreak. While I could make something up whole cloth, the setting already has almost exactly what I would have built.<br /> <br /> You are her greatest piece of work. Art, tool, philosophical statement. She came for you one night, your small village slaughtered, not by the zombies under her, not by the hungry ghosts, by the children. You look back at that night night and remember parents kneeling before their offspring, begging for the knife. You remember a boy &quot;Mother&quot; renamed Adder, staring at a bloody pitch-fork, while his father choked out what a good lad he was. You remember your mother. Cursing you out as you cried, stained carving knife in hand. An entire village sacrificed itself for its children. But <i>your</i> mother. Why? Was something wrong with you? Was your life worth so much less than the other kids?<br /> <br /> &quot;Mother&quot; renamed you, she did all the children. It gave you some measure of peace. The girl that was cursed, that was worthless, was dead, she <i>should</i> be dead. You screamed at her every night, cursing her as she deserved. Perhaps that was why you were taken to see &quot;Grandfather&quot;. &quot;Mother&quot; wouldn't tell you. Only that, &quot;Of all my Seeds, you have come closest to the truth&quot;. The trip the &quot;Grandfather&quot; was enlightening. You saw majestic vistas, and grim wonders. The Hand-Bone forest, so large that you would not have thought the whole world could hold it. The slave-trains of the Timeless Order, an endless line shackled together, driven ever forward by the whips of coin-eyed overseers. You saw the sea. Smooth and still as glass. Each galley oar that cut the surface felt like a personal insult to the peace of sea, and you felt somewhat pleased the oarsmen were under the lash. But something felt <i>off</i> about everything. A desperate denial, everything was to much. No-one suffered, they <i>agonised</i>. No-one had hobbies, they had <i>obsessions</i>. It wore you down just to watch.<br /> <br /> As alien as the world outside was, nothing could have prepared you for &quot;Grandfather&quot; himself. You could hear him long before you reach what &quot;Mother&quot; called the Mouth. Pain, hate, desperate to make it stop. By the time you can see him, your thoughts have been soaking in &quot;Grandfather's&quot; pain for days. Face to &quot;face&quot; you did the only thing you could, you took mother from her sheath and cut the screaming out of your head.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;There are more in pain. More that suffer. Is your peace worth so much more than theirs?&quot;</i><br /> &quot;Mother, I... I can't...&quot;<br /> <i>&quot;You can't? You would curse the world to save yourself? What are you worth?&quot;</i><br /> &quot;Nothing&quot;<br /> <i>&quot;What are </i>they<i> worth?&quot;</i><br /> &quot;Nothing&quot;<br /> <i>&quot;What is Nothing worth?&quot;</i><br /> &quot;Everything&quot;<br /> <br /> You allowed yourself a faint smile as you watch the Mound be consumed by Pyre Flame. Your purple dress was stained with ash, the last of the Seeds had stopped screaming, finally at peace. This was the truth &quot;Mother&quot; had taught you. To exist, is to suffer. Your purpose is to remove suffering. But there is so much of it, and so much seems impossible to end. You sigh and turn from the Mound, you couldn't stop until you had saved everyone. You couldn't curse the world for not saving you. You <i>would not</i> become your mother.<br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> Midnight - The Speaker:<br /> One thing I've always felt the sig Abyssals needed, a completely sincere devotee of the Ancestor Cult.<br /> <br /> &quot;He accepted, go and return to your tribe, Axe-Biter-tak, and know you are a true Tear Eater.&quot; The youth looked at the gibbering dead-thing, probably wondering how you knew what he was saying. Still, she didn't question, and strode confidently out of the cave.<br /> <br /> You looked at the deranged Great Dead, &quot;Honestly, Axe, 'She looks tasty' is not a good reason to deny her gift.&quot;<br /> <b>&quot;Braytip yolle givder stek.&quot;</b><br /> &quot;It's an excellent gift, I... don't interrupt... I'm <i>trying</i> to keep your tribe <i>alive</i> you stubborn ass! A warrior that can dive into a first age tomb, <i>alone</i> I might add, isn't someone you waste because you're feeling peckish, and your last food offering was a month ago!&quot;<br /> <b>&quot;Fentig forsate ginriga welam.&quot;</b><br /> &quot;Tell you what, I'll get Biter-tak's sept to burn a captive in your honour as a celebratory gift. How's that?&quot;<br /> <b>&quot;Rel tika.&quot;</b><br /> &quot;Good,&quot; you sigh and shake your head, &quot;Lover preserve, your daughter doesn't give me this much trouble.&quot;<br /> <b>&quot;Tellak dibur.&quot;</b><br /> &quot;Oh, she likes <i>something</i> all.. ahhh, oh shit, gotta go! See you later, Axe-Biter! Celebratory ritual! Planning! Not getting eaten by over-protective fathers! Important things!&quot;<br /> You sprinted out of the cave.<br /> <br /> You stood a little ways off from the celebration, thanks for a new warrior, and a successful raid. The living tribes tribes didn't know how to treat you. You weren't a shaman, yet you spoke with the dead. Not a chieftain, though no sept would gainsay you. You were an anomaly. You helped the living honour those whom came before. You help the dead remember why the living are important. But the Moon-Slaves come. Tongues drip with the gods' poison. Preaching obsequiousness to bullies and tyrants. The armies of the Bull spread ever further. Even the Immaculate Order, with its worship of the Exalted, and praise of effective suicide, comes this far north. The living and the dead must stand together. Or they will surely fall alone.<br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> Daybreak - The Dictator:<br /> Because Emperor Scientist is still close enough to stereotype to work as a sig.<br /> <br /> You could still hear the screaming. It echoed around the halls, the agonised wail of ghosts being smelted together with labyrinth ore. The plates for the Lion's new war machine were coming along nicely, soon this force would be ready for deployment.<br /> <br /> <i>She was beautiful. That was the only way you could describe her. And you </i>wanted <i>her. Oh, how you wanted her. She was presently owned by another, but both her and he were ghosts. And you had advantages over ghosts.</i><br /> <br /> &quot;Proctor, the supply caravans have been ambushed. Forces have been deployed, but it means a delay in...&quot;<br /> The ghost stopped mid-sentence as you looked at him.<br /> &quot;Find who did this, if they are dead, they can replace the lost supplies, if alive, correct it.&quot;<br /> &quot;Yes, Proctor,&quot; The ghost saluted smartly and left.<br /> This delay would be costly. Part of the frame was unstable and needed to be reinforced. This meant more resources would have to be dedicated to maintenance. Silver lining? More time for Necromancy.<br /> <br /> <i>Ghosts they were. But ghosts of obscene power. You had only dabbled in Necromancy before now, the Lion didn't value it much and you found artifice much easier, Necromancy was what was needed. Necromancy and power.</i><br /> <br /> The Legion marched under the bloated red sun. The dry sand cracked underfoot. The nomad tribes of the desert fled before the inevitable march, but they are not the target. The mining city of Gem lies to the north, it will be a city of the dead before next Calibration.<br /> <br /> <i>She hated you. You were sure of that now. It would have been simpler if you could convince her you were a saviour, but Necromancy demands its price. You took out the single most valued object you own, a single black feather. You would prove yourself the Lion's superior, and the Neverborn would give you what once was his. If not? You would take it by force.</i><br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> Day - The Bounty Hunter<br /> No excuse, just think it's cool.<br /> <br /> The knife sunk into the matron's lower spine, severing the cord. She tried to scream as her legs went limp, but no sound escaped the alley. You quickly withdrew and passed the blade along her neck. She wouldn't be found until morning, plenty of time to leave town. Even if you hadn't killed her. No-one trusts a stranger.<br /> <br /> &quot;Here, take a look at this!&quot; You peer over the Prioress' shoulder.<br /> &quot;Ok, I'm looking. What is it?&quot;<br /> She looks at you like you're an idiot. &quot;Isn't it obvious?&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, <i>you're</i> the genius. I just stab things.&quot;<br /> &quot;True, credit where it's due, you are very good at stabbing things.&quot; She giggled.<br /> &quot;So...&quot;<br /> &quot;So, what?&quot;<br /> &quot;What is it?&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, right! This little device is a modification of the Monstrance, while an Exaltation is bound within it enables the possessor to find all the Hun souls that have ever been bound to that Exaltation!&quot;<br /> You blinked at her. &quot;Please tell me you have something in mind for this <i>other</i> than your constant revenge games?&quot;<br /> &quot;Nope.&quot;<br /> &quot;Good grief.&quot;<br /> &quot;Cheer-up, Stabby, you'll get to kill and kidnap more people.&quot;<br /> You sighed, &quot;No worries, boss.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Look, mate. I've been ordered to take you to Cold House <i>alive</i> and <i>mostly</i> intact. Stop screaming before you find out how liberal I can interpret that.&quot; You turned to the burlap sack. &quot;Besides, there's no-one alive in miles, and the dead are on my side.&quot; The man inside suddenly got very quiet. &quot;Thankyou.&quot; So this was you life now. Kidnapping and wetwork for a brilliant, but completely obsessed, dead exalted, at least it paid well. Besides, if they put as much effort into their job they might <i>actually</i> be able to destroy creation. And you <i>like</i> creation. All your toys are here.<br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> Moonshadow - The Prophet<br /> Because, in the end, it all is ashes and dust.<br /> <br /> You smiled at the people around you. &quot;Be at peace my brothers and sisters. For today, we release a dear loved one from the cruelties life have inflicted upon her.&quot; You turn to the elderly woman lying on the table before you. Her body was wracked with disease. &quot;Are you ready sister?&quot;<br /> She coughed, body filling her mouth. She'd be dead in minutes regardless, but this would help the living as much as her. You placed a small bowl below her neck and drew a soulsteel straw. Wiping part of her neck you insert the straw into the vein. The blood flows into the bowl and in moments her eyes close.<br /> &quot;It is done, remember, brothers and sisters, though today we may seem to have lost a friend, she resides now in the Lands of the Dead. Her eyes will shine with the wisdom of her age, her body, hale beyond anything known by the living, but even in death there is hunger, there is thirst. The dead want as the living want, and so the cycle continues.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;In death you have time, honoured one, time to progress further along the path on enlightenment.&quot; You smile at the new ghost, they always needed time to adjust.<br /> &quot;I know, Anagami, I just guess I thought death would come with some inherent revealation,&quot; she laughed, &quot;I suppose I should not be surprised at even the Dead-Land's callousness.&quot;<br /> &quot;If it were easy, we would all have achieved it. I find reciting the Path's End helps when I'm discouraged, perhaps you would care to join me?&quot; She nodded and you chanted together.<br /> &quot;Without good, no evil. Without want, no lack. Without desire, no need. The Absolute is one. And one is the Void.&quot;<br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> Hmm, ran out of steam a little at the end there. But it late, and I'm tied","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As you are now, so once was I,<br /> As I am now, so you will be.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/285-andonno","name":"Andonno","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T05:57:25-07:00","id":668119,"title":"","content":"Yeah he died on duty, I think from illness, and there was something there about whether it's better to shirk your duty and stay in bed if you're ill and live as a result, or do your sworn duty but die from fever as a side effect. I thought that was interesting. Apparently the Lover did too. <br /> <br /> Honestly I wouldn't mind if some Abyssals had the Euro-Gothic look. I think it worked for him. He was kind of a Shakesperean tragic character with that backstory anyway. Just when all of them do, it's tedious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T06:12:37-07:00","id":668155,"title":"","content":"Don't butterflies symbolize death in Japanese culture? I got the idea for an Abyssal who wears a black kimino covered in cherry blossom motifs and who always has butterflies surrounding her. I think someone in Jen's thread had a similar idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T06:26:10-07:00","id":668160,"title":"","content":"I can, and will, continue to believe that Artorias from Dark Souls makes a great Dusk caste. The broken left arm that doesn't seem to encumber him at all, the utter disparity between everyone claiming he's a hero for dying in battle against horrendous forces versus the addled berserker you are forced to fight, the dark aura which almost seems to ooze and leave a trail of inky blackness like a slime trail behind him. The fact they tempered his rage with sorrow (Sif waiting for him in the Abyss and by his grave) and heartbreak (Ciaran mourning over his grave). That's a proper Dusk caste.<br /> <br /> That being said, what needs to come across in a new Dusk sig is the feeling of sorrow. Maiden of the Mirthless Smile was, for her set, seemingly the most willing and delighted to serve the end of existence; I'd want the Dusk in 3e to seem the most <i>despondent</i>, the most unwilling, and yet perhaps the most damned, to serve the Neverborn... or give him a hopespot towards the end. Start with a pair of shortswords or a greatsword, but have him /her be shown, in chapter stories and pictures, to be using a wide assortment of weapons; make it clear to the reader across the breadth of 3e that nothing, and I mean absolutely nothing, cannot be turned into a murder weapon in his/her hands, <i>and he hates himself for this</i>. Give him a face like an Adonis, marred by parallel, linear scar-marks as he he's just sent all morning trying to claw his face off with his own spiky-fingered gauntlets, rather than look at the monster in the mirror one more time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","user":"Brasstreader","date":". 09-17-2015, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T06:30:53-07:00","id":668170,"title":"","content":"I really do not understand this idea that <i>every</i> Abyssal has to be an emo crying every night about how they're serving Oblivion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T06:36:49-07:00","id":668172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668170#post668170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really do not understand this idea that <i>every</i> Abyssal has to be an emo crying every night about how they're serving Oblivion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all of them. Just 1/5. The Midnight might be the most enthusiatic about it, at least in the sense that he gets the best seat on the death-behemoth to preach from while the world ends. He's there for the vista, and the ghost babes. The Daybreak as an investigator, avenging the living and the dead, is awesome; have her be renegade. The Day caste works best for gut-renching psychopath, the one who actually thinks murdering the world is <i>fun</i>. The Moonshadow's there to see the whole process is running on schedule, that the guests of the Master are well-fed, the trains run on time, and the doomsday device goes off at precisely 11:59, Falling Fire 27. But the Dusk makes the best moper.<br /> <br /> If any of the 3e sigs should mope, it's the guy with the nine-foot plank of soulsteel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","user":"Brasstreader","date":". 09-17-2015, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T06:47:34-07:00","id":668178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668170#post668170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really do not understand this idea that <i>every</i> Abyssal has to be an emo crying every night about how they're serving Oblivion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except none of them really are. <br /> <br /> All the canon sigs except Disciple, Prince, and FTP are pretty much one note gleeful psychos. Disciple is pretty one note himself but there is some complexity of character there due to Jade. FTP is, of course, fine. <br /> <br /> It would be nice to have a loyalist who is still serving inspire his distaste and self-inflicted feelings of damnation, feeling like he owes it to whoever saved his life, or something.<br /> <br /> Another nice thing ITT is how the characters are not taking themselves super cereal all the time, that got exhausting with the canon sigs. Only the Alchies, some GSPs, and Sids seemed immune to it. All the Solars were and man was that ever boring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T07:08:21-07:00","id":668186,"title":"","content":"The most Iconic feeling Midnight I ever ran with was a psychotic guy that basically embraced the whole I'm dead thing and became effectively became a Super Zombie. Also extremely good at raising more undead and commanding any dead/undead he encounter to join his hordes.<br /> <br /> I've depict him and a big strong guy, that is far better held together than the typical zombie. If he isn't leading the charge at the head of a horde of zombies he is still with a entourage of zombies or ghosts under his dominance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T07:12:45-07:00","id":668187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andonno</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trench-coat and a fedora?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div> Seems kind of anachronistic, tbh.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T07:21:38-07:00","id":668224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668187#post668187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems kind of anachronistic, tbh.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Exalts are above such mundane worrries like &quot;anachronism&quot;. They instead decide their clothing based on sheer Rule of Cool.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T07:33:03-07:00","id":668231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668224#post668224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exalts are above such mundane worrries like &quot;anachronism&quot;. They instead decide their clothing based on sheer Rule of Cool.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gvdf5n-zI14\" data-code=\"gvdf5n-zI14\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/gvdf5n-zI14/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Lots of more modern looks are definitely off-limits. With investigators, you're aiming for Judge Dee, not Sam Spade. Or, if you're going for a gothic look, an 18th century European magistrate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T07:33:18-07:00","id":668232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668224#post668224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exalts are above such mundane worrries like &quot;anachronism&quot;. They instead decide their clothing based on sheer Rule of Cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Play the game how you like, but can we leave gonzo stuff like this out of -official- material?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T07:37:57-07:00","id":668237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668231#post668231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gvdf5n-zI14\" data-code=\"gvdf5n-zI14\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/gvdf5n-zI14/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Lots of more modern looks are definitely off-limits. With investigators, you're aiming for Judge Dee, not Sam Spade. Or, if you're going for a gothic look, an 18th century European magistrate.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what exactly does an 18th century European magistrate look like?<br /> <br /> To be honest, I prefer to minimise the later European influence. It's not very fantastical for me (being British), and the lesser amounts of European influence is one of Exalted's selling points over games like DnD. Obviously that's subjective though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-17-2015, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T07:38:38-07:00","id":668238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668172#post668172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not all of them. Just 1/5. The Midnight might be the most enthusiatic about it, at least in the sense that he gets the best seat on the death-behemoth to preach from while the world ends. He's there for the vista, and the ghost babes. The Daybreak as an investigator, avenging the living and the dead, is awesome; have her be renegade. The Day caste works best for gut-renching psychopath, the one who actually thinks murdering the world is <i>fun</i>. The Moonshadow's there to see the whole process is running on schedule, that the guests of the Master are well-fed, the trains run on time, and the doomsday device goes off at precisely 11:59, Falling Fire 27. But the Dusk makes the best moper.<br /> <br /> If any of the 3e sigs should mope, it's the guy with the nine-foot plank of soulsteel.</div> </div> </div> </div>in my opinion there should never be a all of this caste must be this and that, it should always depend on the individual.<br /> example of a none psychotic HAPPY dusk caste loyalist is yet another of my comics abyssals so he will be inside this spoiler so no one gets spoiled <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Soulsteel Monsoon, he was a Carmine Lily child (see carmine lily in roll of glorious divinity page 135) since they are seen as bad omens he was left in the woods to die.<br /> He miraculously survived ended up being shunned and hated by one and all.<br /> He became a pit fighter until a rare disease ate away at his strength crippling him and making him into a beggar.<br /> Dying cold and alone in a world that hates him, she appeared...<br /> The daybreak caste known as &quot;Thrice Orphaned Lady of Sorrows&quot; the adopted grand daughter of the deathlord known as &quot;the Craftsman of Genocide&quot; one of the deathlords that make up the Quadrumvirate (an alliance of the four unnamed deathlords).<br /> She did the first nice thing ANYONE had ever done to monsoon, she gave him a friendly pat on the head and a smile.<br /> She was soon attacked by dragon-blooded immaculate monks, as she was busy fighting, one of them Snuck up behind her. <br /> Monsoon used the last of his strength to leap in front of the attack. As he laid there dying he heard the voice of one of the deathlords (the madman of the Arena). He offered Monsoon the chance to be by the Lady of Sorrows side, to defend her from this world that forsake them both. He said yes and have ever since been at Lady of Sorrows side and he's having the time of his life.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T07:55:31-07:00","id":668249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <di