th.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T08:02:03-07:00","id":668252,"title":"","content":"As a thought about how to approach Abyssals- in addition to the Castes, I would vote that each should symbolize a particular 'approach' to playing/portraying Abyssals:<br /> * The Loyalist (cheerfully serving their Deathlord)<br /> * The Malcontent (in service to their Deathlord, but questioning if it's the right thing to do)<br /> * The Rebel (someone actively rebelling against their Deathlord)<br /> * The Pentitent (someone actively seeking redemption as a Solar)<br /> * The Mad (someone outside the Deathlord structure entirely, enthralled in service to Oblivion)<br /> <br /> Rather than forcing the signatures to all be part of a single Circle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T08:02:28-07:00","id":668253,"title":"","content":"now another thing i thought about is, perhaps each individual sig abyssal should perhaps have a theme that fits with the deathlord that he/she serves. It would be interesting to see","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T08:30:16-07:00","id":668287,"title":"","content":"I don't think a redemption-seeker should be presented as a default character. To me that sends the wrong message. Abyssals should stand on their own merit, not &quot;oh you're sad you're not Solars, so here's an out).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T08:36:03-07:00","id":668288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668252#post668252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a thought about how to approach Abyssals- in addition to the Castes, I would vote that each should symbolize a particular 'approach' to playing/portraying Abyssals:<br /> * The Loyalist (cheerfully serving their Deathlord)<br /> * The Malcontent (in service to their Deathlord, but questioning if it's the right thing to do)<br /> * The Rebel (someone actively rebelling against their Deathlord)<br /> * The Pentitent (someone actively seeking redemption as a Solar)<br /> * The Mad (someone outside the Deathlord structure entirely, enthralled in service to Oblivion)<br /> <br /> Rather than forcing the signatures to all be part of a single Circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this, but I think it leaves something out. Not sure where it would fit, but there should be at least one who is like the Harbinger of the Ghost-Cold Wind in the 2E core: I don't even know if he's a loyalist or not, but he represents the &quot;third path&quot; that is neither &quot;destroy the world&quot; nor &quot;redemption.&quot; He's a Lawgiver of the Dead, who makes the living give to the ancestor cults like he believes they should, who protects the dead when nobody else will. I think he sees himself as a Robin Hood figure even when he kills the living in huge numbers -- taking wealth (life) from the rich so they know what it's like to be poor (dead). (Since he can't give actual life back to the dead, he compels the living to give them grave goods and veneration, which they owe to those who worked all their lives to leave their children something to inherit.)<br /> <br /> I think The Mad could be somebody who wants to replace their Deathlord, not as a rebellion against their goals or methods but just because they're not good enough; this Abyssal wants to serve Oblivion or the Neverborn, not some Deathlord who's time is long over.<br /> <br /> The Rebel role could be split between The Mad, and the Penitent. That leaves room for the Lawgiver of the Dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T08:36:29-07:00","id":668289,"title":"","content":"I have an idea for a Pro-Ghost, but Anti-Deathlord Abyssal, but was never clear on where they would stand on Oblivion. Ghost don't seem to like Agents of Oblivion but at the same time, a ghost wouldn't exist if it wasn't for Oblivion?<br /> <br /> To add some background to my character concept, the Crimson Shaman was a shaman of an ancestor worshiping tribe in the East. His tribe has difficulties from some of the local gods who want the tribe to worship them not their ancestors. The gods try to assassinate the shaman and his apprentice, so in desperation Crimson accepts the Deathlord's offer and exalts as a Midnight Caste. Crimson exacts revenge on the gods and the ancestral ghosts of his tribe convince him to abandon his deathlord, leave the tribe, and head to the underworld to be a traveling ronin who helps ghosts out.<br /> <br /> The Crimson Shaman has no desire to destroy Creation, but will violently defend the underworld and any Ancestor worshiping cults. I don't see him having any issues with Solars or wishing to become one. Yet his negative intimacy with the Gods of the Terrestrial Bureaucracy might cause conflict with the Creation based Exalts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 09-17-2015, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T08:38:46-07:00","id":668292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668288#post668288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this, but I think it leaves something out. Not sure where it would fit, but there should be at least one who is like the Harbinger of the Ghost-Cold Wind in the 2E core: I don't even know if he's a loyalist or not, but he represents the &quot;third path&quot; that is neither &quot;destroy the world&quot; nor &quot;redemption.&quot; He's a Lawgiver of the Dead, who makes the living give to the ancestor cults like he believes they should, who protects the dead when nobody else will. I think he sees himself as a Robin Hood figure even when he kills the living in huge numbers -- taking wealth (life) from the rich so they know what it's like to be poor (dead). (Since he can't give actual life back to the dead, he compels the living to give them grave goods and veneration, which they owe to those who worked all their lives to leave their children something to inherit.)<br /> <br /> I think The Mad could be somebody who wants to replace their Deathlord, not as a rebellion against their goals or methods but just because they're not good enough; this Abyssal wants to serve Oblivion or the Neverborn, not some Deathlord who's time is long over.<br /> <br /> The Rebel role could be split between The Mad, and the Penitent. That leaves room for the Lawgiver of the Dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>i think it said somewhere that cold wind was a loyalist, (might have been a servant of the bishop but like i said I'm not 100% sure)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T08:38:56-07:00","id":668293,"title":"","content":"Up to now the formula has been: &quot;just add skulls and bones, and voil\u00e1&quot;.<br /> <br /> I would design abyssal sigs based on their stories, not on real world gothic motifs. For example: lets say there's this marukhani boy who herded horses, and for some unfortunate event was exalted as an abyssal. You can either make him a) a hulking knight in skull filled armor, or b) a righteous devil cowboy underworld champion, no skulls needed, maybe he rides the &quot;ghost&quot; of his dear horse, but it need not br a skelleton horse.<br /> <br /> So in general, no more skulls please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T08:39:48-07:00","id":668294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668289#post668289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an idea for a Pro-Ghost, but Anti-Deathlord Abyssal, but was never clear on where they would stand on Oblivion. Ghost don't seem to like Agents of Oblivion but at the same time, a ghost wouldn't exist if it wasn't for Oblivion?</div> </div> </div> </div>well the specters are the pro oblivion guys, ghosts are just ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T08:46:31-07:00","id":668297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668293#post668293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in general, no more skulls please.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amen to this, as a former Warhammer Fantasy player I've had a lifetime supply.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T08:53:55-07:00","id":668303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668293#post668293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Up to now the formula has been: &quot;just add skulls and bones, and voil\u00e1&quot;.<br /> <br /> I would design abyssal sigs based on their stories, not on real world gothic motifs. For example: lets say there's this marukhani boy who herded horses, and for some unfortunate event was exalted as an abyssal. You can either make him a) a hulking knight in skull filled armor, or b) a righteous devil cowboy underworld champion, no skulls needed, maybe he rides the &quot;ghost&quot; of his dear horse, but it need not br a skelleton horse.<br /> <br /> So in general, no more skulls please.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you saying do away with the &quot;trappings of death&quot; thing entirely then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T08:54:45-07:00","id":668305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668294#post668294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well the specters are the pro oblivion guys, ghosts are just ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So when most ghost see a specter, do they run? Grovel? Try to escape notice? All of the above depending on the ghost?<br /> <br /> I'm asking because last time I brought up this character concept, I was told I couldn't help ghosts, but fight Oblivion because ghosts are part of Oblivion? So I am trying to figure out the whole deal with ghosts and oblivion. <br /> <br /> I get the idea that the average ghost does not like Deathlords because of the whole Soulsteel thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T08:59:42-07:00","id":668323,"title":"","content":"The Midnight who preaches that the living should be servants of the dead. The dead are immortal, they are your ancestors who gave you every thing you have, and they're your more experienced, wiser, more enlightened elders. And guess what! Unlike serving selfish Dragon-Blooded or rich mortals, you actually get to become one of the elite. Not in some theoretical future incarnation that might never happen even if it isn't a lie, but in actually verifiable fact -- you can watch your parents die and become ghosts, and when you speak to them it's clear that they remember their lives.<br /> <br /> But you had better earn your place among the honored dead, or at least live a pious life and die a blameless death. Cowards, suicides, and impious youth who refuse to honor their ancestors become soulsteel.<br /> <br /> Death is inevitable for all the living, so this character can have very much of what Isator Levie describes for the macabre. But they need not be gloomy. The living should not fear death, for rewards will come to those who were pious. The dead/undead are not repulsive, they are the next stage of each human's existence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668287#post668287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think a redemption-seeker should be presented as a default character. To me that sends the wrong message. Abyssals should stand on their own merit, not &quot;oh you're sad you're not Solars, so here's an out).</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand the point but... the signature characters exist to show players the sorts of play styles a splat can support. Just look at the new Solar sigs -- one of them is a Realm loyalist, which is rather bizarre IMO, but apparently a life that you can attempt as an Anathema.*<br /> <br /> Redemption should not be the only option other than &quot;destroy the world,&quot; but it should be shown, up-front, to be a viable story. The Penitent sig wouldn't necessarily to be on the verge of becoming a Solar, attempting explicitly to become one, or even aware it's possible. They could be seeking penitence and redemption for what they've become and what they've done, and on a path that could plausibly be leading them to Redemption.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> * I'm imagining either an attitude of wishing the Realm would stop killing Celestials but supporting the Empire other than that (founded ultimately on hypocrisy, ignorance of what props up the Realm, ignorance of what Solar survival would truly mean for the Realm, or a desire to hugely reform the Realm); or a Reluctant Monster Solar who truly believes they are Anathema (at least to start with), but is determined to help the Realm and Immaculates as long as they can control the &quot;demon&quot; inside, and plans to die nobly and/or suicidally when they feel themselves losing control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-17-2015, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T09:00:36-07:00","id":668325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668303#post668303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you saying do away with the &quot;trappings of death&quot; thing entirely then?</div> </div> </div> </div>i think it's more skulls specifically, btw was the Jiangshi, moonshadow, drawing to your satisfaction?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T09:03:26-07:00","id":668326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668303#post668303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you saying do away with the &quot;trappings of death&quot; thing entirely then?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was thinking that going the whole dead animals/feathers/bones way was a good alternative to Beetlejuice trappings of the dead, but then i realized that that might be stepping on the Lunar's tribal themes a bit. I don't know what to do about that. *shrugs*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T09:16:15-07:00","id":668339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokisenna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668232#post668232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Play the game how you like, but can we leave gonzo stuff like this out of -official- material?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh stop with this pretentious nonsense (with the devs are, unfortunately, going with for 3e because of the whining of a loud minority). It's a game about a bunch of golden heroes who murdered <b>the creators of the universe</b> with kung-fu bureaucrats and motherfuckers with Looms of Fate and colonies of pattern spiders in their bodies.<br /> <br /> This entire game is about being a supremely fucking awesome badass, so I don't understand this recent drive towards removing <b>all</b> the fun over-the-top shit. I'm starting to feel like 3e is going to suck. It's going to have <b>none</b> of the stuff which <i>got me into Exalted in the first place</i> (namely, playing as an over-the-top anime hero with badass powers in shit in a really insane world).<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4801,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","user":"Frostav","date":". 09-17-2015, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T09:16:36-07:00","id":668340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668305#post668305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So when most ghost see a specter, do they run? Grovel? Try to escape notice? All of the above depending on the ghost?<br /> <br /> I'm asking because last time I brought up this character concept, I was told I couldn't help ghosts, but fight Oblivion because ghosts are part of Oblivion? So I am trying to figure out the whole deal with ghosts and oblivion.<br /> <br /> I get the idea that the average ghost does not like Deathlords because of the whole Soulsteel thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>well oblivion is not really what created the underworld, the neverborn where the ones who did, specters come from ghosts staring down into oblivion or using the grandmother void necromancy to create permanent roided up nephwracks.<br /> <br /> basically a specter is a ghost with whispers, whispers seem to be a lot more devastating to the sanity of ghosts than it is to other beings.<br /> hungry ghosts can be seen as specters and mortwrights are pretty much the ghosts of people so messed up that even their hungry ghosts would find them disturbing and monstrous.<br /> <br /> depending on the ghost the reaction would vary, for example if a specter (no matter which type) would go up to one of the captains of Varan's legion, the captain would just snap the offending specter in half, other ghost warriors would most likely try and defend his/her home and loved ones best he/she could.<br /> a majority of the ghosts that serve the deathlords are specters. Hungry ghosts=specters. War ghosts=specters (most of the time), Nemissaries= specters. Mortwrights=specters. Nephwracks= the most powerful of specters.<br /> there are certain ancient ghosts that could potentially fight against the deathlords, they are few but they exist.<br /> another thing that i theorise is that the deathlords can command SPECTERS without any problem, not ghosts. The ghosts they actually have to &quot;convince&quot; the old fashioned way.<br /> <br /> i hope i made sense there, my brains a bit mushy right now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T09:30:57-07:00","id":668360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668339#post668339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh stop with this pretentious nonsense (with the devs are, unfortunately, going with for 3e because of the whining of a loud minority). It's a game about a bunch of golden heroes who murdered <b>the creators of the universe</b> with kung-fu bureaucrats and motherfuckers with Looms of Fate and colonies of pattern spiders in their bodies.<br /> <br /> This entire game is about being a supremely fucking awesome badass, so I don't understand this recent drive towards removing <b>all</b> the fun over-the-top shit. I'm starting to feel like 3e is going to suck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Murdering the creators of the universe required a centuries-long war waged the cooperation of multiple different heroes, and it wasn't a sure thing even with all of what the army of the gods had at its disposal. Without a tremendous risk, there's no drama, no political struggles, and no exciting tales of heroes struggling against the odds. That's why the power levels are being readjusted, that's why there's less of a focus on super-powerful world-enders, and that's why relics of past ages are being made rarer. Even Gurren Lagan eventually had to tone things down in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T09:39:39-07:00","id":668368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668339#post668339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh stop with this pretentious nonsense (with the devs are, unfortunately, going with for 3e because of the whining of a loud minority). It's a game about a bunch of golden heroes who murdered <b>the creators of the universe</b> with kung-fu bureaucrats and motherfuckers with Looms of Fate and colonies of pattern spiders in their bodies.<br /> <br /> This entire game is about being a supremely fucking awesome badass, so I don't understand this recent drive towards removing <b>all</b> the fun over-the-top shit. I'm starting to feel like 3e is going to suck.</div> </div> </div> </div>...because somebody said trenchcoats and fedoras don't look right in a bronze/iron age world?<br /> <br /> I don't believe anyone wants to remove <i>all</i> the &quot;fun over-the-top-shit.&quot; It's just that the amount and kind of FOTTS you have in the game has to be moderated for the setting to stay coherent.<br /> <br /> Have you ever tried to think about the Marvel (or DC) universe as one, collected thing? Comics present a world with all kinds of heroes, coming from all kinds of backgrounds, ostensibly existing in the same space but having curiously little impact on each other or on their world... most of the time. Generally, the root justification for almost everything that happens in those settings is &quot;because it would be cool&quot;, and look what happens: humanoid aliens fighting against gorilla-men in alternate dimensions alongside honest-to-Copperfield wizards and genetically-enhanced supersoldiers. It's all very surreal when you step outside it and stop suspending disbelief for a moment. The worst part is, each individual character's story usually does make some amount of sense on its own, but when you put them all together the differences between them make the collective whole feel implausible.*<br /> <br /> Exalted <i>could </i>be a Fantasy Superheroes game, where everyone just goes crazy with their appearance and abilities and there's no requirement for anything to make sense in the context of the setting around it... but that would be a selling the game a bit short, don't you think? Why would that be <i>more compelling</i> than a game that aspires to be cogent and consistent in its entirety? I don't know about you, but I feel more engaged by stories that I can <b>believe, </b>not just enjoy.<br /> <br /> *<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Disclaimer - this is why I dislike the Justice League. Too often, it feels like big groups of diverse heroes are constrained by the need to... continue being a big group of diverse heroes, which usually means that nobody contributes as much as they are able to or behaves according to the idioms they follow in their personal stories.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's going to have <b>none</b> of the stuff which <i>got me into Exalted in the first place</i> (namely, playing as an over-the-top anime hero with badass powers in shit in a really insane world). </div> </div> </div>Idle curiousity - would you consider &quot;Darker than Black&quot; to be over-the-top? That show is my benchmark for what a coherent superhero anime looks like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 09-17-2015, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T09:50:42-07:00","id":668384,"title":"","content":"Some Exalts wear weird clothing = <i>literally</i> equal to the completely incoherent nonsense that is superhero comics<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T09:55:19-07:00","id":668386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668384#post668384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some Exalts wear weird clothing = <i>literally</i> equal to the completely incoherent nonsense that is superhero comics<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That makes for an interesting line of thought, really. If you were plunking down superheroes into Exalted, you'd have to change their character designs to do it, and make certain compromises in powers and what they were, if making them types of Exalted. The Question is no exception. Accordingly, the Modern Shard would also change things around, and did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T10:01:51-07:00","id":668398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668384#post668384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some Exalts wear weird clothing = <i>literally</i> equal to the completely incoherent nonsense that is superhero comics.</div> </div> </div> </div>//Correction: indiscriminate_FOTTS.equals(completely incoherent nonsense that is superhero comics).<br /> <br /> Mainly, my objection is that if you have some unusual element for a character - clothes, powers, personal outlook, etc. - and I ask &quot;Why?&quot; and the <i>only</i> answer you can come up with is &quot;OOC, I think it's cool,&quot; then that punches a hole in the setting. I try to discourage people from punching holes in the setting - too many holes in the setting makes it hard to tell good stories, and usually efforts to patch holes in the setting just make it look worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T10:20:09-07:00","id":668430,"title":"","content":"What if the Sig Moonshadow was emulating the Dual Monarchy somehow? He could be someone trying to build a nation that bridges Creation and the Underworld. It's probably too much to ask that the sig moonshadow is a pair of twins given exhalations, while one dresses in black and the other in white, Conjoined twins would probably be offensive and more than a little tasteless (plus WW did that in vampire already).<br /> <br /> OH! Tumor babies! Maybe the moonshadow has dots in Underworld Familiar that manifest as one or more tumor babies that can detach themselves and crawl around to spy for him.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://nathanbiberdorf.files.wordpress.com/2015/01/not-a-baby-im-a-tumor.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T10:22:16-07:00","id":668433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668339#post668339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">with the devs are, unfortunately, going with for 3e because of the whining of a loud minority.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or perhaps that they think certain things don't fit the aesthetic of the game they're designing?<br /> <br /> Nah you're right it's gotta be due to our massively successful Echo Chamber Letter-Writing Campaign. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668339#post668339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm starting to feel like 3e is going to suck. It's going to have <b>none</b> of the stuff which <i>got me into Exalted in the first place</i> (namely, playing as an over-the-top anime hero with badass powers in shit in a really insane world).</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://img.4plebs.org/boards/tg/image/1383/94/1383941704711.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T10:22:26-07:00","id":668434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668293#post668293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in general, no more skulls please.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I love the no-skull rider, the notion of no-skulls-at-all feels constraining.<br /> Skulls are okay. Just not <i>mandatory</i>. Skulls-optional.<br /> To that effect, black-optional, white-optional, greyscale-optional, and blood-stains optional.... (ok, blood-recommended_still_optional).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","user":"Brasstreader","date":". 09-17-2015, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T10:53:15-07:00","id":668465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668398#post668398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mainly, my objection is that if you have some unusual element for a character - clothes, powers, personal outlook, etc. - and I ask &quot;Why?&quot; and the <i>only</i> answer you can come up with is &quot;OOC, I think it's cool,&quot; then that punches a hole in the setting. I try to discourage people from punching holes in the setting - too many holes in the setting makes it hard to tell good stories, and usually efforts to patch holes in the setting just make it look worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or maybe my character thinks its cool and is a <b>demigod with nearly-infinite potential</b> so he gets to do whatever the fuck he wants.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668433#post668433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or perhaps that they think certain things don't fit the aesthetic of the game they're designing?<br /> <br /> Nah you're right it's gotta be due to our massively successful Echo Chamber Letter-Writing Campaign.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://img.4plebs.org/boards/tg/image/1383/94/1383941704711.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div><i>Exalted is a game where one of your main antagonists is Death, Creator of the Underworld. Except there's several of him, probably six or seven. Oh, and he's got 13 dread henchmen, one of whom was probably you at some point in time. Also, Hell has a personal grudge against you this time. Did I mention Magical America regularly trains and sends ninjas out for you personally? Ninjas specially trained in ass-kicking? Which, if they won't work, they keep giant robotic suits of armor on reserve for. Oh, and the Transformers have united under Omicron, and are invading. The Jedi have corrupted Heaven and usurped your rightful place as the Masters of Everything. Your ex-wife just dropped by, and she's a two thousand year old shape-changing man-eating monster now, interested in maybe going on a date next Thursday. Your best friend from your last life and while growing up now seeks to cover all the lands of Middle Earth in darkness, if he can just find this damn ring. And your God has the world's biggest crack habit, and needs some serious rehab.</i> \u2014Darius Solluman<br /> <br /> I'm talking about the above.<br /> <br /> The above quote is <b>the</b> quote which made me go out and grab 2e's core rulebook. Unfortunately, the Creation which drew me in has been slaughtered by the devs in the name of their boring-as-hell 3e version. All good things come to an end, I guess.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T10:55:46-07:00","id":668469,"title":"","content":"lets all get back on track and wait for it's release until we love or hate 3e","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T11:01:36-07:00","id":668482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668465#post668465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Exalted is a game where one of your main antagonists is Death, Creator of the Underworld. Except there's several of him, probably six or seven. Oh, and he's got 13 dread henchmen, one of whom was probably you at some point in time. Also, Hell has a personal grudge against you this time. Did I mention Magical America regularly trains and sends ninjas out for you personally? Ninjas specially trained in ass-kicking? Which, if they won't work, they keep giant robotic suits of armor on reserve for. Oh, and the Transformers have united under Omicron, and are invading. The Jedi have corrupted Heaven and usurped your rightful place as the Masters of Everything. Your ex-wife just dropped by, and she's a two thousand year old shape-changing man-eating monster now, interested in maybe going on a date next Thursday. Your best friend from your last life and while growing up now seeks to cover all the lands of Middle Earth in darkness, if he can just find this damn ring. And your God has the world's biggest crack habit, and needs some serious rehab.</i> \u2014Darius Solluman</div> </div> </div> </div>My description of Exalted lives!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T11:06:12-07:00","id":668489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668465#post668465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe my character thinks its cool and is a <b>demigod with nearly-infinite potential</b> so he gets to do whatever the fuck he wants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why does your character think it's cool? What would lead them to the idea of making one-of-a-kind costumes to begin with? &quot;I'm doing it because I can&quot; is not a reason. Most often, I see it used as an excuse not to consider or to avoid admitting what the actual reason is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668465#post668465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Exalted is a game where one of your main antagonists is Death, Creator of the Underworld. Except there's several of him, probably six or seven. Oh, and he's got 13 dread henchmen, one of whom was probably you at some point in time. Also, Hell has a personal grudge against you this time. Did I mention Magical America regularly trains and sends ninjas out for you personally? Ninjas specially trained in ass-kicking? Which, if they won't work, they keep giant robotic suits of armor on reserve for. Oh, and the Transformers have united under Omicron, and are invading. The Jedi have corrupted Heaven and usurped your rightful place as the Masters of Everything. Your ex-wife just dropped by, and she's a two thousand year old shape-changing man-eating monster now, interested in maybe going on a date next Thursday. Your best friend from your last life and while growing up now seeks to cover all the lands of Middle Earth in darkness, if he can just find this damn ring. And your God has the world's biggest crack habit, and needs some serious rehab.</i> \u2014Darius Solluman<br /> <br /> I'm talking about the above.<br /> <br /> The above quote is <b>the</b> quote which made me go out and grab 2e's core rulebook. Unfortunately, the Creation which drew me in has been slaughtered by the devs in the name of their boring-as-hell 3e version. All good things come to an end, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you took Darius' quote at face value instead of seeing it as a comical exaggeration, I can see why you'd be disappointed. That said, 2E didn't really live up to that insane depiction either, so I'm mildly confused as to why you're only beginning to get upset now.<br /> <br /> In any edition, gonzo gameplay is more than possible if that's the kind of story you want to tell. The question is, should that be the default presentation that the books provide?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T11:12:50-07:00","id":668496,"title":"","content":"Look, 1d4chan's descriptions of everything in every RPG are willfully and hyperbolically distorted and bloated on years of recursive memes, which means they only bear the slightest resemblance to the actual game in question. I've had players that want to literally play Jedi in heaven and who have gotten pissed that Sidereal charms aren't actual force powers and that they don't actually have ligthsabers because of that description.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T11:23:40-07:00","id":668513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668465#post668465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm talking about the above.<br /> <br /> The above quote is <b>the</b> quote which made me go out and grab 2e's core rulebook. Unfortunately, the Creation which drew me in has been slaughtered by the devs in the name of their boring-as-hell 3e version. All good things come to an end, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're taking a hyperbolic meme super serious that is your issue, not the game's. <br /> <br /> Pretty funny to me that you're decrying 3e as boring before its release, with minimal detail. All you're putting forth is a lot of conclusory baseless assumptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T11:28:14-07:00","id":668517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668339#post668339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This entire game is about being a supremely fucking awesome badass, so I don't understand this recent drive towards removing <b>all</b> the fun over-the-top shit. I'm starting to feel like 3e is going to suck. It's going to have <b>none</b> of the stuff which <i>got me into Exalted in the first place</i> (namely, playing as an over-the-top anime hero with badass powers in shit in a really insane world).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>While I'll miss the crazy over the top Exalted of Second Edition, I will disagree that the entire game is about being fucking awesome badass. There is so much more to Exalted that Punching mountains into dust. There is a whole rich mythology of back stabbing gods, scheming alien Yozi, and your run of the mill ambitious bandit lord out there. I mentioned this back in the Duck Selling thread: The crazy magitech drew my interest to Exalted, but the Celestial Politics kept my interest.<br /> <br /> When Third Edition drops, your second edition books aren't going to spontaneous combust. The Devs aren't going to come to your house, beat you up, and piss all over your Infernal splat book. You can still have crazy Heroin Pissing Dinosaurs in your game. Third edition may set the base line of crazy lower, but frankly, I never needed help bringing the crazy to the gaming table. My Pathfinder game saw my PCs getting high off of strange alien substances. In the Skype Game I'm playing in, we have a doom train run by a death lord.<br /> <br /> I'm not too worried about Third Edition. It will bring much needed sanity to the rules and setting. Hell, according to some of the spoilers I saw, Solars are going to be doing some CRAZY shit at Essence two. So maybe the crazy isn't going away. It's just going to be your character doing the crazy instead of some NPC.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> Oh, shit! Just realized that you are basing your idea of Exalted off of a Meme. We are talking about two different levels of crazy. Not even 2nd edition can touch that meme's level of crazy. That is the main reason why you are getting a lot of backlash on the forums. The game you want to play doesn't exist in that form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 09-17-2015, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T11:38:03-07:00","id":668524,"title":"","content":"sigh