ly a specter is a ghost with whispers, whispers seem to be a lot more devastating to the sanity of ghosts than it is to other beings.<br /> hungry ghosts can be seen as specters and mortwrights are pretty much the ghosts of people so messed up that even their hungry ghosts would find them disturbing and monstrous.<br /> <br /> depending on the ghost the reaction would vary, for example if a specter (no matter which type) would go up to one of the captains of Varan's legion, the captain would just snap the offending specter in half, other ghost warriors would most likely try and defend his/her home and loved ones best he/she could.<br /> a majority of the ghosts that serve the deathlords are specters. Hungry ghosts=specters. War ghosts=specters (most of the time), Nemissaries= specters. Mortwrights=specters. Nephwracks= the most powerful of specters.<br /> there are certain ancient ghosts that could potentially fight against the deathlords, they are few but they exist.<br /> another thing that i theorise is that the deathlords can command SPECTERS without any problem, not ghosts. The ghosts they actually have to &quot;convince&quot; the old fashioned way.<br /> <br /> i hope i made sense there, my brains a bit mushy right now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Cool. So it is entirely possible to find a middle ground between helping ghosts continue their existence in relative peace and fighting the forces of oblivion. <br /> <br /> I would like to see more variation among Abyssal Signature characters. For example:<br /> <br /> &quot;I hate my deathlord, but serving him is better than personally destroying the ones I love&quot;<br /> &quot;I left my deathlord because he is prolonging the suffering of Creation with his political schemes.&quot;<br /> &quot;I don't want to tear down ALL of creation, just the Realm. 