v><br /> It is less this and more this is a topic about Abyssals. It might be a good idea to start a new topic, since a lot of people have opinions on how over the top Exalted should be.<br /> <br /> Back on topic,<br /> <br /> Wastevens, I like your character concepts, since they include intimacies. I think Abyssals need more Intimacies and be less Psychopathic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 09-17-2015, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:12:24-07:00","id":668591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668570#post668570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Shit, this guy's got an opinion that goes against the groupthink! Shut him down for the crime of thinking differently!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If the divergent topic of &quot;how much exotic crazy stuff should Exalted have?&quot; is so important to you, start a new thread about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:13:28-07:00","id":668604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668570#post668570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Shit, this guy's got an opinion that goes against the groupthink! Shut him down for the crime of thinking differently!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This thread began as a spinoff from the discussion of taking Abyssal Loyalists seriously, because it made Xanroth think about something but he didn't want to derail the discussion.<br /> <br /> Sometimes thread topics drift organically, but in this case it seems a lot of people still want to talk about potential Abyssal sigs. Nobody is stopping you from creating a thread about to what degree over-the-top sensibilities belong in Exalted. I guarantee you that lots of folks will be along to engage with you. There's no reason to play the martyr for free speech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:17:51-07:00","id":668610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668570#post668570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &amp;quot;Shit, this guy's got an opinion that goes against the groupthink! Shut him down for the crime of thinking differently!&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody is gonna stop you from creating another thread to discuss your desire to play memexalted. It just has nothing to do with this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:18:51-07:00","id":668613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668568#post668568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking my own suggestion on 'How to Abyssal Sig'<br /> Here\u2019s my suggestions:<br /> * The Bloody-Handed General (Loyalist):<br /> A Daybreak Caste who specializes in mass combat. In life, she served as a distinguished general for the Perfect of Paragon, with a distinguished career. Not the most personally martially inclined (although no slouch in a fight), she was more noted as being a brilliant tactician and strategiest, inventing new gambits and often anticipating her opponents traps and counter-trapping them. She lived for the praise and the limelight, easily acquired in her youth and middle age; lost when she was forced into retirement. Old now, a fever took her\u2026<br /> <br /> Except the First and Forsaken Lion knows talent when he sees it. The Blood-Handed General is one of his most loyal servants, leading the Lion\u2019s war machine against their neighbors, and basks in the adulation of her immortal troops.<br /> <br /> * The Fourth Terror of Night Eternal (Malcontent)<br /> A Day Caste who specializes in inspiring revolutions. In life, he was a nobody; a slave-farmer in a village near Whitewall, he had no great aspirations. That changed when a priest-magistrate from the city came through his village, seizing the salt and supplies needed for his family to survive the winters for repairing the Great Northern Road. He struck the magistrate, and was summarily hanged by his guards, his goods and family forfeit to the City of Whitewall for striking it\u2019s representative. As he was dancing on the impromptu gallows, he heard the Bishop of the Chalcedony Thurible whisper an offer- join me and you will have your vengeance.<br /> <br /> Since that time, The Fourth Terror of Night Eternal has moved through Whitewall, finding the desperate, the criminal, the forgotten of that sterile city, and spreading seditious words. Additionally, he walks more openly under a false name as a foreign prince, nominally representing the interests of a distant land while encouraging the upper classes to grow only more brutal, paranoid and repressive. Bloody revolution that will crack the walls of Whitewall and leave the city ripe for the taking seems to be only a matter of time.<br /> <br /> But The Fourth Terror has a weakness now; he has fallen in love with a young nobleman who works in charity for the underclasses. At first he tried to divert his love away from his mission, but now finds himself questioning it entirely; he well knows the pain and destruction that will accompany this revolution, and is certain his lover will perish in those flames. He continues for the moment, but with far less fervor than before.</div> </div> </div> </div>i like those, mind giving a small description of how you think they should look? like what's the &quot;theme&quot; on their appearance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:22:27-07:00","id":668616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668570#post668570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Shit, this guy's got an opinion that goes against the groupthink! Shut him down for the crime of thinking differently!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Oh you want to be shut down? Please leave the thread. </b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:33:48-07:00","id":668626,"title":"","content":"is it safe to come out now?... sigh, i made this thread to have some fun discussions, cool ideas, a source of different things to draw and to get some social interaction for once... and it turns into a brawl so bad it needed a moderator to calm it down... now i'm just sad <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> anyhow let's get back to the original purpose now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:35:41-07:00","id":668631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668568#post668568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* The Fourth Terror of Night Eternal (Malcontent)<br /> A Day Caste who specializes in inspiring revolutions. In life, he was a nobody; a slave-farmer in a village near Whitewall, he had no great aspirations. That changed when a priest-magistrate from the city came through his village, seizing the salt and supplies needed for his family to survive the winters for repairing the Great Northern Road. He struck the magistrate, and was summarily hanged by his guards, his goods and family forfeit to the City of Whitewall for striking it\u2019s representative. As he was dancing on the impromptu gallows, he heard the Bishop of the Chalcedony Thurible whisper an offer- join me and you will have your vengeance.<br /> <br /> Since that time, The Fourth Terror of Night Eternal has moved through Whitewall, finding the desperate, the criminal, the forgotten of that sterile city, and spreading seditious words. Additionally, he walks more openly under a false name as a foreign prince, nominally representing the interests of a distant land while encouraging the upper classes to grow only more brutal, paranoid and repressive. Bloody revolution that will crack the walls of Whitewall and leave the city ripe for the taking seems to be only a matter of time.<br /> <br /> But The Fourth Terror has a weakness now; he has fallen in love with a young nobleman who works in charity for the underclasses. At first he tried to divert his love away from his mission, but now finds himself questioning it entirely; he well knows the pain and destruction that will accompany this revolution, and is certain his lover will perish in those flames. He continues for the moment, but with far less fervor than before.</div> </div> </div> </div>This guy is really cool. Why the Bishop, though? This kind of Abyssal doesn't really seem to be his style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:42:47-07:00","id":668661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668613#post668613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i like those, mind giving a small description of how you think they should look? like what's the &quot;theme&quot; on their appearance?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll repost this, since it got lost:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668326#post668326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking that going the whole dead animals/feathers/bones way was a good alternative to Beetlejuice trappings of the dead, but then i realized that that might be stepping on the Lunar's tribal themes a bit. I don't know what to do about that. *shrugs*</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you differentiate between a Shaman Abyssal and a Shaman Lunar? The only thing I can think of is &quot;The Abyssal is Dirtier and More Bloody&quot;, but I rather have more than the Nosferatu option.<br /> <br /> Acatl from Obsidian and Blood has a good Abyssal look:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://www.blackgate.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/12/obsidian-blood.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:51:15-07:00","id":668676,"title":"","content":"Re: Appearance<br /> <br /> The Bloody-Handed General I see as an older (like, early 50s) but attractive woman. Her hair is silver, her eyes are red. She wears a light soulsteel breastplate and carries a soulsteel dire lance on the field, but prioritizes mobility and being able to communicate over fighting personally (she likes the lance because she can use it for flags and is almost always mounted). She is always accompanied by a talon of crack war-ghosts and skeletal attendants. When her anima is flaring, it glows dark blue- save her hands, which burn with a terrible red light. As her anima intensifies, the red light around her hands solidifies into spectral blood, staining the ground black. Her iconic totem is a murder of ravens, which seek out corpses on the field to pick at the dead flesh.<br /> <br /> The Fourth Terror Of Night Eternal<br /> He looks like John Barrowman circa Arrow. A master of disguise (for moving between the over and underclasses), he prefers to dress in crushed black velvet and white silks, and will always have a flower of some variety on his person if he can manage it. He has become fastidious about his appearance, fussing over makeup and hair coloring and keeping his nails trimmed. His anima burns grey, wrapping around him like a fog cloud- his location is unmistakeable, but it is difficult to see his details, the fog growing thicker even as it grows brighter. His iconic totem is a rat.<br /> <br /> Re: Why the Bishop?<br /> <br /> Honestly, because I'm trying to put one of the sigs in each cardinal Direction, and the Bishop seems like he could use some love in the North. Is their a better fit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:52:47-07:00","id":668677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668661#post668661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'll repost this, since it got lost:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> How would you differentiate between a Shaman Abyssal and a Shaman Lunar? The only thing I can think of is &quot;The Abyssal is Dirtier and More Bloody&quot;, but I rather have more than the Nosferatu option.<br /> <br /> Acatl from Obsidian and Blood has a good Abyssal look:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://www.blackgate.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/12/obsidian-blood.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>personally I don't think it needs to have a direct difference, perhaps that the abyssals wear more bones and has more blood than a lunar shaman, possibly doing things more &quot;wastefully&quot;.<br /> Like making torturous sacrifices and things like sacrificing and wasting the last cattle in a starving village, possibly being more aggressive than a lunar shaman would be.<br /> In my head the stereotypical lunars shaman would be more of a slowly let people adapt to my way whilst an abyssal would lead a band of nephwracks into the village, then have nemesaries posses the children of those that oppose him and make them eat their own parents alive...<br /> <br /> yeah he works, ooooh another thing i just thought up is that abyssals can use hidden necrotech as a part of their outfit, lets say that we give him a belt that looks like it's the skeletal remains of a snake, except it can come alive and act as a sort of living poisonous spear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:57:21-07:00","id":668682,"title":"","content":"I honestly don't like Necrotech as a system and i hope it's not going to remain in 3e. To me it always seemed like someone looked at magitech and decided to use corpses and necromancy in an attempt to be clever and edgy. You want fancy tools? IMO, they either need to be Artifacts or actual undead creatures, not some crossover fusion thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:59:42-07:00","id":668685,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that belt (which is a cool idea!) doesn't need to be given the name &quot;necrotech.&quot; That's just a badass artifact spear with Evocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T13:02:03-07:00","id":668689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668676#post668676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Appearance<br /> <br /> The Bloody-Handed General I see as an older (like, early 50s) but attractive woman. Her hair is silver, her eyes are red. She wears a light soulsteel breastplate and carries a soulsteel dire lance on the field, but prioritizes mobility and being able to communicate over fighting personally (she likes the lance because she can use it for flags and is almost always mounted). She is always accompanied by a talon of crack war-ghosts and skeletal attendants. When her anima is flaring, it glows dark blue- save her hands, which burn with a terrible red light. As her anima intensifies, the red light around her hands solidifies into spectral blood, staining the ground black. Her iconic totem is a murder of ravens, which seek out corpses on the field to pick at the dead flesh.<br /> <br /> The Fourth Terror Of Night Eternal<br /> He looks like John Barrowman circa Arrow. A master of disguise (for moving between the over and underclasses), he prefers to dress in crushed black velvet and white silks, and will always have a flower of some variety on his person if he can manage it. He has become fastidious about his appearance, fussing over makeup and hair coloring and keeping his nails trimmed. His anima burns grey, wrapping around him like a fog cloud- his location is unmistakeable, but it is difficult to see his details, the fog growing thicker even as it grows brighter. His iconic totem is a rat.<br /> <br /> Re: Why the Bishop?<br /> <br /> Honestly, because I'm trying to put one of the sigs in each cardinal Direction, and the Bishop seems like he could use some love in the North. Is their a better fit?</div> </div> </div> </div>oooh i like it, ill see if i can take a crack at drawing the bloody handed general tomorrow, i apologize in advance since i'm not great at drawing people that looks slightly older (or well i haven't really had an opportunity to try yet but still) and i may end up with a silly breastplate since i'm still trying to figure out how to keep the silhouette without making it into a boobplate... anyhow if you find any picture that you think would work as a reference for either her body or armor or both go ahead and link it and i will gladly use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T13:03:13-07:00","id":668701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668682#post668682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don't like Necrotech as a system and i hope it's not going to remain in 3e. To me it always seemed like someone looked at magitech and decided to use corpses and necromancy in an attempt to be clever and edgy. You want fancy tools? IMO, they either need to be Artifacts or actual undead creatures, not some crossover fusion thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the reduction of magitech i expect the Deathlords' dark industries to resemble fantasy more than a magic industrial revolution except with skulls. <br /> <br /> I mean I think spine chains and stuff like that work just fine. I actually love the one comic where Black Physician is directing repairs on a giant necro rhino.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T13:22:02-07:00","id":668742,"title":"","content":"Spine chains, necro rhinos, the corpses of 77 soldiers stitched together into a giant zombie ogre and all that work just fine as actual statted creatures. I just dislike the point buy build a monster workshop systems.<br /> <br /> But ugh, &quot;Daybreak bringing his Zombie Rhino in for repairs the same way I'd bring my truck into a car mechanic to get my oil changed&quot;? UUUUUGH.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T13:30:12-07:00","id":668751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668303#post668303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you saying do away with the &quot;trappings of death&quot; thing entirely then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, but the trappings of death should be more diverse. You know, different cultures relate death with different things. The vietnamese who were taken care of at american hospitals after the war were freaked out by seeing everyone dressed in white, a color they associated with death. Something similar happens with the &quot;skull formula&quot;, maybe most westerners would see a skull insignia and think abouth death and lethality, but here in my country, we have candy skulls, we laugh at death two days a year and the idea of having your loved ones come back from the death during those days is a comforting one, not a terrifying one.<br /> <br /> So I say that a flower themed abyssal may be ultra-cool if his/her background explains how his homeland has this &quot;death-flower&quot; they use to bury their dead. Or an abyssal that's accompanied by a &quot;flock&quot; of hawks and eagles (and not necessarily ravens and black birds) based on the idea of sky burials.<br /> <br /> The trappings are fine, as long as they mean more than &quot;huh, they dress all goth and shit mom&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":90,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.co