":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T19:48:51-07:00","id":669149,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Howl of Oblivion</b></span><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.wired.com/images_blogs/magazine/2010/12/pl_games_deadspace23_f.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Some Deathlords seek out great souls to lead their armies, the Eye and Seven Despairs instead creates them. Scream of Oblivion is not one, but several mortals who dared to oppose the Deathlord. Over the course of weeks, he fused them together though painful and laborious occult surgeries. When he felt his work was finished, he offered them a deal: take the black exaltation or spend the rest of their existence as his test subject.<br /> <br /> The creature known as the Howl of Oblivion still contains the knowledge of the five mortals used to make it, but its mind has been broken and warped.<br /> It and its servants sweep through areas like a plague, gorging themselves on the living and then moving on. Eventually, Howl of Oblivion becomes bored with its feasting and simply abandons its created minions to wander the South in isolation.<br /> <br /> Howl of Oblivion wavers between moments of angry confusion and those of relative lucidity. Other deathknights have learned engage Howl of Oblivion only when its mind is (relatively) stable. At those times, the creature has proven to be a knowledgeable ally. One wonders what might happen if Howl\u2019s mind were ever made whole and healthy again, for it has often expressed a deep hatred toward the Deathlord who created it.<br /> <br /> As for Eye and Seven Despairs, he views Howl of Oblivion as something of a failed experiment. He had hoped to make a deathknight superior to those already on hand, not one who spends most of its time as a gibbering horror. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T21:30:33-07:00","id":669209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=668742#post668742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spine chains, necro rhinos, the corpses of 77 soldiers stitched together into a giant zombie ogre and all that work just fine as actual statted creatures. I just dislike the point buy build a monster workshop systems.<br /> <br /> But ugh, &quot;Daybreak bringing his Zombie Rhino in for repairs the same way I'd bring my truck into a car mechanic to get my oil changed&quot;? UUUUUGH.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jesus you people really <b>do</b> want to get rid of <i>every single</i> cool thing in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T22:02:20-07:00","id":669244,"title":"