lay into a topic for a few hours, instead of two-minute grunts on fantasy football (or 'degenerate American rugby' for my Commonwealth and global-football allies)?<br /> I ain't even mad.... mostly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T07:45:02-07:00","id":670948,"title":"","content":"Most of the people I work with can barely speak English, and in a Communist country you've got to be careful talking about controversial topics anyhow. It's nice to discuss things with people who know what words like &quot;sociology&quot; actually mean.<br /> <br /> Not that I necessarily want to have really heavy discussions: there's a reason I'm not a mod on two political forums anymore (and I only had to moderate the European Politics section, not the American Politics or Religion sections... shudder).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-19-2015, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T08:01:15-07:00","id":670953,"title":"","content":"have a dusk caste. this one is based of a concept i made.<br /> Unbound Brutality of War.<br /> sorry brasstreader no redemption seeking dusk this time, instead i got the picture in my head of a dusk caste that fights as the champion of an army of the dead instead of being it's general (especially since we already have a general drawn here so).<br /> <br /> bloody big picture again.<br /> link is in the first post.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://img08.deviantart.net/bd8d/i/2015/262/6/9/unbound_brutality_of_war_by_xanroth-d9a4f65.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I may have gone a bit over the top with his design here and there, but i promise it all has some sort of purpose. enjoy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T08:20:07-07:00","id":670975,"title":"","content":"So there's &quot;Putting severed human hands and eyes on a necklace,&quot; and then apparently there's &quot;An entire dead person in lieu of a personal banner.&quot; Wow.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if it's supposed to be a real corpse, and a Dusk strong enough to fight while carrying one ... but imagine this:<br /> <br /> An Abyssal has a child's corpse in a noose hanging from his back like a personal banner. Their own armor and weapons are attuned, so this is really the only significant weight they carry, and it's tied to their back at the waist so it doesn't swing around. Let's say that it has knives impaling its hands and feet, too. Pretty demoralizing sight for the living, right? And a sort of extra layer of armor.<br /> <br /> Then somebody gets close enough to try to stab the guy in the back or grab him from the side, and discovers that <i>the child-corpse is a zombie</i> that suddenly lashes out with those knives to defend its creator.<br /> <br /> <br /> I feel kinda ashamed and horrified that I came up with that. O.O<br /> I'm going to blame Xanroth for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-19-2015, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T08:22:47-07:00","id":670979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=670975#post670975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there's &quot;Putting severed human hands and eyes on a necklace,&quot; and then apparently there's &quot;An entire dead person in lieu of a personal banner.&quot; Wow.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> like i said, it has a purpose. It does make quite an impression seeing someone using an entire person as his banner <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />...<br /> and aye, i did kind of go over the top with it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T08:35:45-07:00","id":670991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=670975#post670975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there's &quot;Putting severed human hands and eyes on a necklace,&quot; and then apparently there's &quot;An entire dead person in lieu of a personal banner.&quot; Wow.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if it's supposed to be a real corpse, and a Dusk strong enough to fight while carrying one ... but imagine this:<br /> <br /> An Abyssal has a child's corpse in a noose hanging from his back like a personal banner. Their own armor and weapons are attuned, so this is really the only significant weight they carry, and it's tied to their back at the waist so it doesn't swing around. Let's say that it has knives impaling its hands and feet, too. Pretty demoralizing sight for the living, right? And a sort of extra layer of armor.<br /> <br /> Then somebody gets close enough to try to stab the guy in the back or grab him from the side, and discovers that <i>the child-corpse is a zombie</i> that suddenly lashes out with those knives to defend its creator.<br /> <br /> <br /> I feel kinda ashamed and horrified that I came up with that. O.O<br /> I'm going to blame Xanroth for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Insert sparkely eyes gif here... that is AN AMAZING IDEA!<br /> if i wasn't afraid of getting in trouble for drawing stuff involving dead mutilated kids I would draw that thing.<br /> it is an absolutely magnificent thing to have on an abyssal <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> i had a few thoughts about making it so that the corpse would be able to move around and things but i never thought about the knifes.<br /> You're good at this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> disclaimer. I know i may be sounding like a raving maniac &lt;.&lt;, &gt;.&gt;. but I'm actually a pretty nice person... i just have tendency to make pretty horrifying characters...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":4455,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","user":"Xanroth","date":". 09-19-2015, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T10:56:58-07:00","id":671130,"title":"","content":"There was... I think Omicron who made a magical girl Modern Exalted? Anyways, IIRC the Abyssal had a jiangshi chauffeur/bodyguard and also carried around a coffin with some necrotech horror on her back that she just opened up when excrement impacted propeller. I'm probably remembering that wrong, but I like the image anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T11:36:04-07:00","id":671161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=670531#post670531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that about 80% of what I dislike about that comic is the blase attitude the (presumably) mortal technician has with interacting with the Daybreak.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about that bothered you?<br /> <br /> Personally I see it as being fairly human. You work around someone enough and you kind of subconsciously forget how special they are til the anima starts flaring and they start bending portcullis bars with their bare hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T13:13:50-07:00","id":671229,"title":"","content":"Hm.<br /> <br /> I'm gonna get in on this thread.<br /> <br /> By which I mean as soon as I'm done with this week's Boot strip, I'm gonna whip up some random Abyssal pictures and let y'all come up with backstories for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T13:19:37-07:00","id":671231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=671229#post671229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm.<br /> <br /> I'm gonna get in on this thread.<br /> <br /> By which I mean as soon as I'm done with this week's Boot strip, I'm gonna whip up some random Abyssal pictures and let y'all come up with backstories for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>yaaaaay <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T15:32:22-07:00","id":671362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=670531#post670531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh<br /> <br /> I think that about 80% of what I dislike about that comic is the blase attitude the (presumably) mortal technician has with interacting with the Daybreak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seven-Degreed Physician is pretty nice as Abyssals go, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> I mean, look at that smile.<br /> <img src=\"http://vignette4.wikia.nocookie.net/thirdexalt/images/a/a3/Physician_of_Black_Maladies-0.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/566?cb=20141013070010\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T15:59:28-07:00","id":671400,"title":"","content":"I definitely think that there's a point at which people discussing practical solutions to problems or collaborating on implementing those solutions should take a straightforward, pragmatic approach. After reading Seeing Like a State, I developed this image of a scene opening on a Solar king crouching down to comb through the soil with their fingers while a local farmer casually lays out what the recent problems have been and the king make out-loud observations and aside questions... I've grown attached to it as an idea of what a Solar who's genuinely for the people would be doing. Similarly, accounts of people like Napoleon or von Blucher exchanging ribald jibes with the rank and file, asking after their conditions, occasionally tasting their rations. It's... warm. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that about 80% of what I dislike about that comic is the blase attitude the (presumably) mortal technician has with interacting with the Daybreak.</div> </div> </div> </div> What's the alternative?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T16:21:18-07:00","id":671465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=671400#post671400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What's the alternative?</div> </div> </div> </div>probably something like:<br /> the mortal technician cowering in fear and respect whilst constantly referring to the Daybreak by some title or sobriquet or something is my guess. (I don't like this alternative myself)<br /> <br /> but I actually like that comic because to me its the juxtaposition between mystery and mundanity: to me its mysterious but to them, its normal and mundane and I like it for that. when I want to see a setting, I want to know whats normal for that setting so I can know what the baseline is and how to interact with it in a day to day manner- exceptional circumstances are well that: exceptional circumstances. my reactions to those circumstances are formed from them happening in game and deviating from the normal living. to me its awesome something like that can be mundane, because it shows how people can consider anything mundane and its only when we look sideways at it all and realize that we're currently communicating cross vast distances using devices no larger or smaller than books while also using them to play videos and games that we realize how awesome the thing is when we mostly take it for granted.<br /> <br /> to me its saying &quot;I'm a mortal technician, and I'm so used to this horrific undead stitching stuff and whatnot, that when a Daybreak comes up to and asks for help with it, I'm like whatever, because I'm that cool. Sure any lesser guy would be cowering in the corner, but me, I've been doing this for years, you learn to get used to it, because I'm so cool, I can find this boring. Making undead monstrosities, talking with Daybreaks, gathering up dead parts? just another day on the job. I deal, thats all.&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm sure there are spirit exorcists out there who stop being all fearful or emotional about their job to. Not everyone gets super-emotional and invested into everything they just learn to live with it and get things done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T16:23:51-07:00","id":671466,"title":"","content":"If it was a scene from Alchemicals and the Deathknight was a Champion I would have zero problem with that scene.<br /> <br /> As is, the The Seven-Degreed Physician of Black Maladies is a deathknight with Charisma 1, Compassion 1, a penchant for torture, forced body modification and taking villagers full of people and slowly vivisecting them one at a time while the others watch so he can build a spine chain from their corpses. Outside of the mentioned torture, he has zero social skills beyond four dots in manipulation to mitigate his awfulness. He lives in a Manse that he calls the Sanatorium Sepulchral that is <i>literally</i> his evil lair.<br /> <br /> Having a mortal or ghost assistant speak to him the same way my mechanic would speak to me when telling me that my truck has some damage and it will take a week to get a part in to fix it strains my credulity past it's breaking point. Maybe it would sit better with me if he was torturing the guy or his family because he didn't follow the deathknight's orders on how to repair the rhino zombie. Maybe a better scene would be him teaching enslaved ghosts how to be necrosurgeons by having them practice on their own corpses first. Maybe a better Necrosurgury comic would be the guild delivering a bunch of slaves to his Sanatorium Sepulchral and the majordomo signing off on their receipt and when someone refers to them as slaves the majordomo responds with &quot;They aren't slaves, they're <i>supplies</i>&quot; as some stitched up zombie monsters come out to drag them down to the laboratories.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of ways the Necrosurgury chapter comic could have gone and I think &quot;Deathknight brings his Rhino in for a check up&quot; was boring and immersion breaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T17:45:20-07:00","id":671534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=670953#post670953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">have a dusk caste. this one is based of a concept i made.<br /> Unbound Brutality of War.<br /> sorry brasstreader no redemption seeking dusk this time, instead i got the picture in my head of a dusk caste that fights as the champion of an army of the dead instead of being it's general</div> </div> </div> </div>Not redemption-seeking; that implies he thinks there's even such a thing as redemption for the puppies he's hugged to death accidentally, let alone the entire graveyards he's filled at the call of his terrible eldritch masters. He's just sad that his life now amounts to a hit list until the world ends, when he died protecting a village from raksha, since the Deathlords kidnapped his daughter and let him see her based on how many puppies he's murdered this week.<br /> {joke's on him, that's a neomah in the cage. They turned the daughter into his breastplate; <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/UnstoppableRage\" target=\"_blank\">he's</a> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/BerserkerTears\" target=\"_blank\">gonna be</a> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/RoaringRampageOfRevenge\" target=\"_blank\">so pissed</a>}<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> bloody big picture again.<br /> link is in the first post.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://img08.deviantart.net/bd8d/i/2015/262/6/9/unbound_brutality_of_war_by_xanroth-d9a4f65.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I may have gone a bit over the top with his design here and there, but i promise it all has some sort of purpose. enjoy </div> </div> </div>.... no. no, no no. This could actually work.<br /> Maybe we don't need a moper, after-all.<br /> Good work. This is....<br /> I'm gonna need a character sheet. And some rum. Both spiced, and regular. Or vodka.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T17:55:31-07:00","id":671543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=671229#post671229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm.<br /> <br /> I'm gonna get in on this thread.<br /> <br /> By which I mean as soon as I'm done with this week's Boot strip, I'm gonna whip up some random Abyssal pictures and let y'all come up with backstories for them.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://img14.deviantart.net/d3d2/i/2015/113/5/4/jolly_cooperation_by_hellsing4682-d6vt7vp.png\" target=\"_blank\">And now, this day has meaning. Yes. Come soon, provide your art, and aid us in jolly cooperation!</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T00:18:51-07:00","id":671699,"title":"","content":"So here's an Abyssal. The whole &quot;Tibetan Sky Burial&quot; thing spoke to me, so that's the aesthetic I went for.<br /> <br /> I'll leave it up to you lot what his name and Caste end up being, but whatever he is rest assured that he and that bird are Eternal Bros. Deathlord asks him to kill the bird? He ditches the Deathlord.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://orig08.deviantart.net/c778/f/2015/263/f/b/abyssal_exalt_by_flyingspiderstudios-d9a8dr3.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T00:48:53-07:00","id":671704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=671699#post671699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So here's an Abyssal. The whole &quot;Tibetan Sky Burial&quot; thing spoke to me, so that's the aesthetic I went for.<br /> <br /> I'll leave it up to you lot what his name and Caste end up being, but whatever he is rest assured that he and that bird are Eternal Bros. Deathlord asks him to kill the bird? He ditches the Deathlord.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://orig08.deviantart.net/c778/f/2015/263/f/b/abyssal_exalt_by_flyingspiderstudios-d9a8dr3.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>sweet work there guru, he looks awesome and so does the bird. I would say day caste for him,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T00:50:21-07:00","id":671705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=671534#post671534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not redemption-seeking; that implies he thinks there's even such a thing as redemption for the puppies he's hugged to death accidentally, let alone the entire graveyards he's filled at the call of his terrible eldritch masters. He's just sad that his life now amounts to a hit list until the world ends, when he died protecting a village from raksha, since the Deathlords kidnapped his daughter and let him see her based on how many puppies he's murdered this week.<br /> {joke's on him, that's a neomah in the cage. They turned the daughter into his breastplate; <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/UnstoppableRage\" target=\"_blank\">he's</a> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/BerserkerTears\" target=\"_blank\">gonna be</a> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/RoaringRampageOfRevenge\" target=\"_blank\">so pissed</a>}<br /> <br /> .... no. no, no no. This could actually work.<br /> Maybe we don't need a moper, after-all.<br /> Good work. This is....<br /> I'm gonna need a character sheet. And some rum. Both spiced, and regular. Or vodka.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I will be looking forward to seeing the the result of the vodka, rum and character sheet <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> also thank you very much <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":4455,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","user":"Xanroth","date":". 09-20-2015, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T01:29:10-07:00","id":671715,"title":"","content":"so, i may have figured out a bit of backstory and info on brutality now, let me know what you think of it.<br /> <br /> He serves under the first and forsaken lion.<br /> <br /> He was the champion/executioner of a minor kingdom in the south.<br /> He was chosen for his great size and strength, later on he showed his lord that he was not just a big brute but an expert in psychological warfare.<br /> However after loosing a important battle his king ordered him bound in chains and locked in a dark room.<br /> Above him drops of water would fall on him (barely enough to keep him from dying, not nearly enough to quench his thirst) and delicious food where placed just out of reach (he was feed a few scraps of it after it had cooled down and become disgusting to taste).<br /> It was in this darkness that he would have faded away...<br /> The First and Forsaken Lion had other plans though.<br /> The man that was to become Brutality, was offered a chance to once again rampage across the battlefield this time serving a master that was worthy of his loyalty.<br /> Brutality accepted and thus now he was once more free, he left the burning ruins of the city he had once bleed and committed atrocities for to serve the one that freed him from his prison, the one that made him Unbound!<br /> <br /> here's a bit of picture discussion so to speak.<br /> At first i had thought about giving brutality a couple of manacles around his wrists with broken chains, i dropped that idea, he does however still have a metal choker around his neck that was once attached to a wall in his prison.<br /> the two metal plates that are attached to his shoulders are either there as punishment or he had them attached himself as a sort of vow that until he has managed to free his master from his metal prison he will have the metal plates attached.<br /> the gallows on his back is a pretty horrifying artifact, it works kind of like those torture cages in Yu-Shan, except the victim only needs to have the noose around his/her neck(it only works when the noose is tightened around the victims neck and once it is it burns in such a way that no one can keep it on voluntarily, so no using it to become immortal in battle).<br /> The gallows is used to punish those that dare to betray the Lion, making brutality a walking reminder to all who serve the lion of what will happen to them if they dare to betray him.<br /> The last part just felt fitting, because even though the deathlords relations with the deathknights is supposed to be that of pupil and master (if i have understood it correctly) not that of slave and master.<br /> It felt fitting for the lion to have some way of reminding his servants exalted or not that he's the Lion, not a kitten and those that forget it gets to hang from brutality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T02:57:21-07:00","id":671743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=671534#post671534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna need a character sheet. And some rum. Both spiced, and regular. Or vodka.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would you spice a character sheet? Don't you know the worms can smell it from miles away?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T07:30:06-07:00","id":671885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=671743#post671743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you spice a character sheet? Don't you know the worms can smell it from miles away?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just walk without rhythm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T08:10:58-07:00","id":671956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=671885#post671885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just walk without rhythm.</div> </div> </div> </div>New character concept: Crane stylist Rider of Shai-Hulud. Hookswords and floating about without actually touching the ground. It works perfectly!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T08:20:43-07:00","id":671958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=671956#post671956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> New character concept: Crane stylist Rider of Shai-Hulud. Hookswords and floating about without actually touching the ground. It works perfectly!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> nah that's a lunar Crane stylist with a crane totem - who just always flies<br /> <br /> <br /> As for abyssal sigs...<br /> <br /> I can sadly only really think of 3 core archetypes<br /> <br /> 1) the deathlord loyalists - your usual &quot;lets kill everything forever&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) the psycho - too nuts for deathlords, but neverborn like their moxie so they get to kill everything (even deathlords) forever<br /> <br /> 3) the rebel - doesn't agree with the two above for some reason, usually trying to become a solar","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T09:00:02-07:00","id":672046,"title":"","content":"and here we go one last abyssal for now.<br /> <br /> since we have had 3 males and 2 females in all of the sigs i believe, I decided to make the last one a female day caste.<br /> <br /> say hello to &quot;She who Hunts with Darkness&quot;...<br /> <br /> colored, big and possibly bloody picture.<br /> link in the first post.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://pre06.deviantart.net/fdb4/th/pre/i/2015/263/0/b/she_who_hunts_with_darkness_by_xanroth-d9a9o3j.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> so i got some feedback about the last two from a friend mentioning that he wished they where colored, so i decided to make this one colored.<br /> She who Hunts with Darkness is a day caste, her death was at the hand of a city lunar so in a mockery of the tattooed man that murdered her she wears foul mockeries of the moonsilver tattoos lunars bear. Similar to lunar tattoos, hers is a tale.<br /> A tale of a huntress that will hunt down the very moon itself.<br /> Either at her side or riding in her shadow is a group of underworld beasts that she have trained.<br /> She is able to hide her tattoos and eyes with charms.<br /> She is a huntress. Her hunting grounds are the streets of cities, her hounds are the underworld beasts that follow her and her spear is the very darkness itself.<br /> So beware all whom dare light up the night, for not even shadows are safe from the darkness!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T13:31:29-07:00","id":672336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=671699#post671699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So here's an Abyssal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I can't think of a name, but I do know this: that bird had cracked open his bones and was eating his marrow when he Exalted. It refused to leave him alone afterward, until finally they became bros.<br /> <br /> Also, his bow is strung with the love he felt for the man who betrayed him. He smiles more often now that he keeps it <i>there</i> instead of in his heart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T13:37:38-07:00","id":672340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having a mortal or ghost assistant speak to him the same way my mechanic would speak to me when telling me that my truck has some damage and it will take a week to get a part in to fix it strains my credulity past it's breaking point.</div> </div> </div> </div> The way ahead is clear; we need to find some awful person to introduce to your mechanic so they can commission their services, so you can witness first hand how irrelevent somebody's personality can be to being commissioned for a job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T15:41:45-07:00","id":672414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=672336#post672336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I can't think of a name, but I do know this: that bird had cracked open his bones and was eating his marrow when he Exalted. It refused to leave him alone afterward, until finally they became bros.<br /> <br /> Also, his bow is strung with the love he felt for the man who betrayed him. He smiles more often now that he keeps it <i>there</i> instead of in his heart.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, this I like!<br /> <br /> This next one's an old picture (of an NPC of mine I used as an antagonist for the PCs in an old game), but it might as well get some renewed use here. Feel free to come up with some backstory for this guy. He's called the Bold Marauder Adorned in Alabaster, but that's all we know about him.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://pre14.deviantart.net/0a72/th/pre/i/2015/110/f/0/the_bold_marauder_adorned_in_alabaster_by_flyingspiderstudios-d8qfkpz.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 09-20-2015, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T15:54:42-07:00","id":672430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=672340#post672340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The way ahead is clear; we need to find some awful person to introduce to your mechanic so they can commission their services, so you can witness first hand how irrelevent somebody's personality can be to being commissioned for a job.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is me not liking the comic such an issue?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T17:22:09-07:00","id":672552,"title":"","content":"We need a similar topic for alchemicals. Man do those guys lack a unifying aesthetic...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T04:15:48-07:00","id":673052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=671466#post671466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it was a scene from Alchemicals and the Deathknight was a Champion I would have zero problem with that scene.<br /> <br /> As is, the The Seven-Degreed Physician of Black Maladies is a deathknight with Charisma 1, Compassion 1, a penchant for torture, forced body modification and taking villagers full of people and slowly vivisecting them one at a time while the others watch so he can build a spine chain from their corpses. Outside of the mentioned torture, he has zero social skills beyond four dots in manipulation to mitigate his awfulness. He lives in a Manse that he calls the Sanatorium Sepulchral that is <i>literally</i> his evil lair.<br /> <br /> Having a mortal or ghost assistant speak to him the same way my mechanic would speak to me when telling me that my truck has some damage and it will take a week to get a part in to fix it strains my credulity past it's breaking point. Maybe it would sit better with me if he was torturing the guy or his family because he didn't follow the deathknight's orders on how to repair the rhino zombie. Maybe a better scene would be him teaching enslaved ghosts how to be necrosurgeons by having them practice on their own corpses first. Maybe a better Necrosurgury comic would be the guild delivering a bunch of slaves to his Sanatorium Sepulchral and the majordomo signing off on their receipt and when someone refers to them as slaves the majordomo responds with &quot;They aren't slaves, they're <i>supplies</i>&quot; as some stitched up zombie monsters come out to drag them down to the laboratories.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of ways the Necrosurgury chapter comic could have gone and I think &quot;Deathknight brings his Rhino in for a check up&quot; was boring and immersion breaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like your ideas, but man is that character ever one-note as fuck.<br /> <br /> Physician reads like a D&amp;D necromancer entry much better than he does any kind of nuanced Exalted character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 09-21-2015, 07:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T07:37:29-07:00","id":673155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=671699#post671699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So here's an Abyssal. The whole &quot;Tibetan Sky Burial&quot; thing spoke to me, so that's the aesthetic I went for.<br /> <br /> I'll leave it up to you lot what his name and Caste end up being, but whatever he is rest assured that he and that bird are Eternal Bros. Deathlord asks him to kill the bird? He ditches the Deathlord.<br /> <br /> *snip image*</div> </div> </div> </div>I just wanted to call this guy out as being super awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T07:39:52-07:00","id":673158,"title":"","content":"Hrm. The Tibetian Sky Burial thing gives me an idea for another axis to pursue in Abyssal Sigs; 5 different approaches to the Trappings of Death thematics- which could help with making Abyssals less 'ALL SKULLS ALL THE TIME'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T07:58:42-07:00","id":673168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=673158#post673158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hrm. The Tibetian Sky Burial thing gives me an idea for another axis to pursue in Abyssal Sigs; 5 different approaches to the Trappings of Death thematics- which could help with making Abyssals less 'ALL SKULLS ALL THE TIME'</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... The first Abyssal that my players met in my last (western) campaign was part of a culture that threw their dead out in the ocean tied to huge blocks of carved stone, after a lengthy ceremony when they were painted with sand from their island of birth.<br /> <br /> In keeping with that, the Black Sail of Unfurled Destiny appears to have bone-white skin due to the sand now fused to her skin, and uses a rope with carved funeral stones as her belt no matter what she wears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T13:04:13-07:00","id":673361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=672552#post672552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We need a similar topic for alchemicals. Man do those guys lack a unifying aesthetic...</div> </div> </div> </div>.......0_o<br /> <br /> Honestly, as an Alchemicals fan, thats not really my problem with them. just the opposite: its a little hard to come up with things to make my specific Alchemical different in some way from all the rest....especially when I'm not sure what kind of heroism would happen in Autochthonia that would allow them to exist in the first place....I mean sure there are examples but the entire pint /of Autocthonia is that everything is a little samey because communism.....that and they're all metallic robots using lots of tech, thats a pretty unifying aesthetic right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T14:57:39-07:00","id":673453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=673052#post673052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like your ideas, but man is that character ever one-note as fuck.<br /> <br /> Physician reads like a D&amp;D necromancer entry much better than he does any kind of nuanced Exalted character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depth for the other characters comes from their passions, and relationships, and their culture, how their current life circumstances, and their ideals, and that they have autonomy to decide how to react to a given situation.<br /> <br /> It seems like those aren't things the Deathknights have tended to have a lot of, or a lot of diversity in, frankly. (I approve of Gonzo's post where the character is at least someone specific from somewhere specific who happens to have been raised up by the Powers of Death, and not &quot;some scary guy from somewhere&quot; who meets some trope, and is there for you to fight and has a cool costume.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T15:24:38-07:00","id":673464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=673453#post673453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depth for the other characters comes from their passions, and relationships, and their culture, how their current life circumstances, and their ideals, and that they have autonomy to decide how to react to a given situation.<br /> <br /> It seems like those aren't things the Deathknights have tended to have a lot of, or a lot of diversity in, frankly. (I approve of Gonzo's post where the character is at least someone specific from somewhere specific who happens to have been raised up by the Powers of Death, and not &quot;some scary guy from somewhere&quot; who meets some trope, and is there for you to fight and has a cool costume.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Eeh, Signature characters have a bit more on their shoulders than other characters. They need to illustrate *stuff* about the game, both individually and collectively; essentially, you *have* to back fill your stories for them a bit.<br /> <br /> That said, it's not an excuse for one note, one dimensional characters; just that starting from a blank sheet of paper isn't neccesarily the best approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T00:52:08-07:00","id":673928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=673361#post673361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that and they're all metallic robots</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually highlights one of the more common problems.<br /> By default they're not supposed to be all that metallic, people seem to get rather badly mislead by the shirtless and unadorned look of Stern Whip of Industry and overlook the fact that his appearance is heavily defined by his charm purchases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T01:15:00-07:00","id":673932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=673928#post673928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This actually highlights one of the more common problems.<br /> By default they're not supposed to be all that metallic, people seem to get rather badly mislead by the shirtless and unadorned look of Stern Whip of Industry and overlook the fact that his appearance is heavily defined by his charm purchases.</div> </div> </div> </div>oh him? you mean the red jade alchemical guy? I wasn't talking about him, he is one the least robotic of them all. the soulsteel guy who looks like he is in armor is the robotic one, if anything Stern Whip is bad because he is too <i>human. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T02:30:35-07:00","id":673982,"title":"","content":"Actually, <i>Dreadful Adjudicator of Law </i>is wearing armour. He's an albino-looking bishounen underneath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T02:39:02-07:00","id":673985,"title":"","content":"huh, you learn something new everyday. I thought the showoff soulsteel guy was someone different from the strict judge dredd reference soulsteel guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T02:50:15-07:00","id":673995,"title":"","content":"The showoff and the the Law <i>are</i> different people. They just both happen to be pretty boys, though very different strains of pretty boy. <i>Adjudicator</i> is this cold, seemingly emotionless type who also happens to be in love with a dissident (and the peaceful life offered by his own cover identity).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T13:00:06-07:00","id":674494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=673932#post673932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Stern Whip is bad because he is too <i>human. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>No he's bad because he's <i>misleadingly</i> human.<br /> He looks like a Jade statue (or one of the Metal Men) and a lot of people don't realise that's specifically his thing as an icon of the populat (he's actually more armoured than Adjudicator) rather than a more general Alchemical thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T13:14:20-07:00","id":674525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=673052#post673052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like your ideas, but man is that character ever one-note as fuck.<br /> <br /> Physician reads like a D&amp;D necromancer entry much better than he does any kind of nuanced Exalted character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since Abyssals are picked by their Deathlords, you could say that Physician's Deathlord searched for someone completely terrible to give an Exaltation to. There are people who are all around horrible. Except I believe that the Physician's Deathlord is the Knight one. The one who wants to trade with Creation and spread his influence that way, and tends to be darkly noble and such.<br /> <br /> Tangentally, I read the Physician's write-up last night, and apparently as a mortal he was doing sophisticated cosmetic surgery and organ transplants. That seems out of sync with the technology level of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T13:44:52-07:00","id":674563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=674525#post674525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tangentally, I read the Physician's write-up last night, and apparently as a mortal he was doing sophisticated cosmetic surgery and organ transplants. That seems out of sync with the technology level of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does when you put it that way, doesn't it? I figured he was the go-to guy when you wanted to, for example, harvest the organs from albino conjoined twins because they're part of some magical recipe that requires a very difficult procedure to remove and/or the donors to survive the removal. Or some other horrible cynis wants to have someone render a number of slaves into quadriplegics who's arms and legs are replaces with an array of sex toys - something that no legitimate doctor on the blessed isle is really going to do because it's TERRIBLE and would ruin their legitimate business.<br /> <br /> Basically he's the creation of <i>that one player</i> who marathoned Hellraiser the night before session zero of the abyssal campaign and wanted to play Pinhead, but Infernals hasn't been released yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T16:01:08-07:00","id":674663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=673361#post673361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and they're all metallic robots using lots of tech, thats a pretty unifying aesthetic right there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they are not. They are described as being made of some sort of clay. Their bones are metallic and many of their charms are installed externally. And I think that's whe things go meh... most alchemicals look like people who bathed in glue and walked through a junkyard. The soulsteel guy doesnt look robotic to me, hes just wearing armor. But hey, I'll argue no more about alchemicals here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T16:15:19-07:00","id":674670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=674563#post674563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically he's the creation of <i>that one player</i> who marathoned Hellraiser the night before session zero of the abyssal campaign and wanted to play Pinhead, but Infernals hasn't been released yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a great criteria for an abyssal sig I think. If somebody came to session zero with this character, how likely is it that people would want to kick him out? Again, like with how to take loyalists seriously, a lot of that might be presentation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T16:28:53-07:00","id":674680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=674670#post674670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's actually a great criteria for an abyssal sig I think. If somebody came to session zero with this character, how likely is it that people would want to kick him out? Again, like with how to take loyalists seriously, a lot of that might be presentation.</div> </div> </div> </div>aye, if he's slaughtering hundreds just for shits and giggles then he's going to end up pretty dull.<br /> <br /> If he however have a &quot;reason&quot; to his/her atrocities it can make the character all that more interesting/terrifying.<br /> <br /> A abyssal that murders and mutilates people in horrifying and gruesome ways and calling his &quot;work&quot; art is going to be a bit more interesting than one that just did it because he/she felt like it.<br /> <br /> The deathlords are intelligent, they would most of the time(looking at you mask of winters) not recruit an uncontrollable maniac that will ruin any and all operations unless he/she is distracted by killing.<br /> <br /> as for kicking someone out for their concept, well it depends. I can stomach a lot of stuff but if i see that the rest of the group is uncomfortable then ill just tell said player that he/she should cut the descriptions short so to speak (aka no need to describe in detail how you force feed a baby to it's mother or peel someone like a potato).<br /> If said person can't deal with that, well then that person will have to go i guess since it's unreasonable to not respect your fellow players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T16:39:14-07:00","id":674682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=674494#post674494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No he's bad because he's <i>misleadingly</i> human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Y'all gotta remember, Raziere doesn't <i>like</i> humans, despite being one.<br /> <br /> Raziere has stated she thinks they're boring, and loses interest in playing a character as soon as we remind her that the character is human.<br /> <br /> I don't see the logic in it, mind, but she's been nothing but consistent on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T18:11:05-07:00","id":674762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=674670#post674670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's actually a great criteria for an abyssal sig I think. If somebody came to session zero with this character, how likely is it that people would want to kick him out? Again, like with how to take loyalists seriously, a lot of that might be presentation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly it depends on the player - I've played with people who would skeeve me out with that concept and others who wouldn't","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T18:22:19-07:00","id":674768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=674525#post674525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Abyssals are picked by their Deathlords, you could say that Physician's Deathlord searched for someone completely terrible to give an Exaltation to. There are people who are all around horrible. Except I believe that the Physician's Deathlord is the Knight one. The one who wants to trade with Creation and spread his influence that way, and tends to be darkly noble and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find when it comes to talking about sig characters, the Watsonia perspective is not very useful. The Doylist one is the relevant one, because these characters are being made for the reason of presenting an example to players, and thus those examples should be well-developed, interesting, not shallow...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=674525#post674525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tangentally, I read the Physician's write-up last night, and apparently as a mortal he was doing sophisticated cosmetic surgery and organ transplants. That seems out of sync with the technology level of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah nobody is going to accuse Scroll of Exalts of good writing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T18:35:11-07:00","id":674775,"title":"","content":"This remains one of my favourite uses of Necrosurgery in other media. <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ehNddAPLH3g\" data-code=\"ehNddAPLH3g\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ehNddAPLH3g/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div> There's an even better one from the same series but the horror show there can't be conveyed in one video.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 09-22-2015, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T19:21:55-07:00","id":674798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=674682#post674682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Y'all gotta remember, Raziere doesn't <i>like</i> humans, despite being one.<br /> <br /> Raziere has stated she thinks they're boring, and loses interest in playing a character as soon as we remind her that the character is human.<br /> <br /> I don't see the logic in it, mind, but she's been nothing but consistent on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its complicated to explain. Its like saying that the person is like everyone else and nothing special at all. When I'm trying to make this exceptional hero of legend here.<br /> <br /> That and I don't see how humans have any inherent value- <b>people</b> have inherent value because of their minds, their souls, their inner beauty but not their physical body. I like people. But not this strange obsession people have with a certain form of known as humanity, even if they are the only known form of people. that and to place value on somebody only for their physical body is shallow.<br /> <br /> its just how I see the world....I look more at patterns, connections, dualities, and other such things rather than look at things as they relate to humanity. I have learned how to see the world in more human/social terms to make sure I can interact with it well and live my life, but fundamentally, I'm still approaching it from a point of view where I feel a bit like an alien trying to make sense of a strange planet, because honestly to me everyone else IS strange (I don't think I'll ever get why people do ceremonies or other similar formal things in the real world). I would love to go on about my high-functioning autism and what the theory is behind its thought processes, but thats not really the subject of this thread isn't it?<br /> <br /> Yes we're supposed to be talking about Abyssals, and certainly not this or the Alchemicals. I apologize for derailing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T00:22:25-07:00","id":674982,"title":"","content":"It's not about our physical bodies*, Raziere - if it were, we wouldn't consider the disabled to be fully human (admittedly, for a disturbing length of history, that's exactly what happened). If or when uploading your brain into the Internet becomes a thing, you'll be human, too. <br /> <br /> In fact, considering how the questions of &quot;is that thing human?&quot; and &quot;is it okay to kill that thing?&quot; have gone hand-in-hand for most of human history, I'd say &quot;humanity&quot; is more linked to our concept of personhood than it is to the biological classification of <i>Homo sapiens sapiens</i>. Neanderthals were human, and if the mutants from the <i>X-Men</i> comics were real, they'd be human too.<br /> <br /> *It's silly to pretend that there's a difference between our minds and our physical bodies, so I'm not going to in this post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T01:08:59-07:00","id":675018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=674982#post674982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not about our physical bodies*, Raziere - if it were, we wouldn't consider the disabled to be fully human (admittedly, for a disturbing length of history, that's exactly what happened). If or when uploading your brain into the Internet becomes a thing, you'll be human, too.<br /> <br /> In fact, considering how the questions of &quot;is that thing human?&quot; and &quot;is it okay to kill that thing?&quot; have gone hand-in-hand for most of human history, I'd say &quot;humanity&quot; is more linked to our concept of personhood than it is to the biological classification of <i>Homo sapiens sapiens</i>. Neanderthals were human, and if the mutants from the <i>X-Men</i> comics were real, they'd be human too.<br /> <br /> *It's silly to pretend that there's a difference between our minds and our physical bodies, so I'm not going to in this post.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well thats just another thing I don't understand:<br /> <br /> Why use the word &quot;human&quot; as opposed to &quot;person&quot;? I get that you use it that way, but I don't see why its so often used as a shorthand for some norm of personhood within our species. Particularly in relation to the word &quot;Inhuman&quot;. Often &quot;Inhuman&quot; is equated with immoral or insane behavior and thus humanity is somehow equated with moral behavior. You could argue that hypothetically there might be inhuman behavior that could be moral, but I have yet to find any evidence in this world that anyone considers any inhuman behavior to be moral. Morality itself is a human construct under this consideration and thus is defined around human needs and desires.<br /> <br /> Thus it shows a bias towards our own species, disturbingly similar to how a culture's view of morality would be biased around themselves. Now you may think it silly because no alien species have ever been discovered- negative information does not prove or disprove that aliens exist- But for some reason, my mind is uncomfortable with tying morality to the biases of a single sapient species.<br /> You cannot accuse an alien or a robot of being &quot;Inhuman&quot; as they were never human to begin with and therefore cannot make a moral judgement based on the word &quot;human&quot;. To me any moral judgement based solely on humanity rather than personhood in general is suspect, as what exactly is important enough about humanity as opposed to personhood to judge someone on the former rather than the latter?<br /> <br /> Is it the morality aspect? Why then would one say &quot;your inhuman&quot; as opposed to &quot;your immoral&quot;? if humanity is nothing but another word for morality, why used humanity at all? What exactly is the difference? Is it the sanity aspect? Why then not say &quot;your insane&quot;? Why not say &quot;when you upload your brain you'll be a person too?&quot; It doesn't make any sense to me. Now I may be arguing semantics, but I think its morally important that we be moral for the sake of personhood in general rather than just humanity, if that makes any sense to you. I hope I'm explaining myself clearly, and I still apologize for this.....perhaps we should continue this in PM, Alucard?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T02:35:33-07:00","id":675047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=674525#post674525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since Abyssals are picked by their Deathlords, you could say that Physician's Deathlord searched for someone completely terrible to give an Exaltation to. There are people who are all around horrible. Except I believe that the Physician's Deathlord is the Knight one. The one who wants to trade with Creation and spread his influence that way, and tends to be darkly noble and such.<br /> <br /> Tangentally, I read the Physician's write-up last night, and apparently as a mortal he was doing sophisticated cosmetic surgery and organ transplants. That seems out of sync with the technology level of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Transplants..maybe, especially for a mortal.<br /> Cosmetic Surgery is a lot older than you' think though. Performed by Ancient Indians, Romans and Egyptians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T02:45:35-07:00","id":675059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=674762#post674762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly it depends on the player - I've played with people who would skeeve me out with that concept and others who wouldn't</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's what I meant by the presentation. If it's clearly a creepy guy who wants to live out his fantasy of giving a hooker tentacle breasts and parrot feathers or something then ew. On the other hand if he's playing a character who wants to strike a balance between respect for human bodies and harvesting the un-needed remains of the dead to save the lives of the living, and in extreme cases making monsters because sometimes you need monsters, then cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T02:57:36-07:00","id":675082,"title":"","content":"Here's one thing I'd like to hear if anyone else does.<br /> <br /> Do anyone give their deathknights a look fitting the &quot;Theme&quot; of their deathlord (custom and canon)?<br /> for example, the deathlord known as &quot;the madman of the arena&quot; a warrior and combatant through and through.<br /> This guy is more or less a combat glutton (he became a deathlord because the neverborn promised him the greatest battle of his (un)life if he joined them).<br /> so as a theme since his base of operations is a Colosseum looking arena, I designed his deathknights to have a gladiatorial look about them (oh and he only uses dusk castes and despise archery type weapons).<br /> Have anyone else done that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T07:10:05-07:00","id":675203,"title":"","content":"Playing around with some visual stuff for sigs. I like the idea of someone who actively rejects a lot of the kind of &quot;gothic&quot; aesthetic of the present crop of sigs. Also, I like the idea of someone who carries the scars of their death flagrantly (that's an arrow scar on his forehead). I dunno if it's a good place to start, but I think it could use some workshopping. I think he needs a facial redesign and body tattoos. But I'd like to see some more things along this aesthetic for sigs, maybe?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/FDQyYHD.jpg?1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Pronounced &quot;Monkey Pie&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/762726-actual-play-the-party-prelude-project\" target=\"_blank\">Find my actual play content here!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/656-monkipi","name":"Monkipi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar656_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"318"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T09:09:32-07:00","id":675307,"title":"","content":"I made a very quick <a href=\"http://bersagliere.deviantart.com/art/Berserker-from-the-Abyss-562039143?ga_submit_new=10%253A1443024058\" target=\"_blank\">sketch</a> of an abyssal concept I would like to share. It's based around the idea of shamanism and that not only man dies but so do everything around him. The guy is a berserk inspired barbarian abyssal (cause not only lunars can have barbaric backgrounds!). He wears the skin and horns of the herbivore, and the saberteeth of its predator. His body is modified by that charm that twists the skeletal frame and protrudes bony spikes, an in his case a pair (or maybe four) of scythes that break the skin of his forearems everytime they &quot;unsheath&quot; (somewhat like that Wolverine all the cool kids talk about). His feet are grotesque and twisted into some kind of horrific hooves giving him the overall aspect of a satyr. A satyr that plays a sad tune with his flute and roams the wilds delivering death. Many Silver Pact shamans have come to meet with this strange creature and have recgnized him as &quot;brother death&quot;. I imagine him as a Day caste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T10:05:04-07:00","id":675339,"title":"","content":"wohoo, we're getting a whole bunch of artists in on this, this makes me happy.<br /> @Monkipi damn that one looks awesome, i like the idea of keeping the scar and having someone that more or less goes screw the trappings of death.<br /> <br /> @Gonzo I really, REALLY like that concept, cool art too. Perhaps he could have some sort of I don't know &quot;minor shapeshifting&quot; ability that only affects him visually but more or less looks like a kind of death based monstrous DBT? Depending on his relation to lunars it could be a sort of charm he developed to &quot;honor&quot; or &quot;mock&quot; the lunars.<br /> <br /> keep up the good work my fellow artists <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T12:15:34-07:00","id":675582,"title":"","content":"While I wouldn't dare to design a full signature character (Not that I don't have any character ideas, they're just unsuitable for sigs), I do want to ask:<br /> Has anyone considered animals? Scavengers like raitons and crows are obvious, as are vultures, though they're less used. And I haven't seen hyenas.<br /> But even predators work - they still spell death to many.<br /> <br /> And then, gods: Anubis, Egyptian god of embalming and funerals, had a jackal head. Nekbet was... well, goddess of vultures with a vulture head. Ammit (the monster that would eat the dead's heart if they were not pure) was a mixture of crocodile, lion/leopard and... hippopotamus (which is only funny for the first moment).<br /> <br /> I'm also kinda reminded of the Discworld novel &quot;Reaper Man&quot;, where Death gets fired, and new deaths based on what various beings believe Death to look like pop up - the death of mayflies, for example, takes the form of a carp.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or, leaving animals, I could also see various plants as &quot;trappings of death&quot;. In Germany, both lilies and violets are common grave decorations. Poisonous plants could work, too, as long as they're poisonous enough - if they just make you sick, then it's probably not enough, but a plant that kills you if you eat it would probably count<b>. </b>Foxgloves, for example, though that might still be the low end of the spectrum.<br /> Poppies because of opium and addiction, for an abyssal following the Lover's methods, though I might have drifted into &quot;Anima Banna&quot; instead of &quot;Trappings of Death&quot; by now &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> And to get entirely derailed within one post (and three edits):<br /> Would an army of zombies and skeletons following you everywhere count as &quot;trappings of death&quot;?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":7262,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","user":"Amakawa Yuuto","date":". 09-23-2015, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T13:00:44-07:00","id":675620,"title":"","content":"I've always considered &quot;trappings of death&quot; to be garments. So..is there some way you can <i>wear</i> your skeleton army?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T13:03:45-07:00","id":675647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=675620#post675620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always considered &quot;trappings of death&quot; to be garments. So..is there some way you can <i>wear</i> your skeleton army?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say if your character is designed like gravelord Nito then i would say that if all those bones that make up your suit are alive then they would count as a sort of army i think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T13:04:41-07:00","id":675653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=675620#post675620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always considered &quot;trappings of death&quot; to be garments. So..is there some way you can <i>wear</i> your skeleton army?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think at least once the phrasing was &quot;Surrounded by trappings of death&quot;, which made it more like decorations to me. Sure, decorations can be on your clothes, but they can also be a hidden shrine-room somewhere in the castle.<br /> <br /> /Edit: Abyssals, page 95: &quot;Deathknights can resist this debilitation if they garb <i>or otherwise surround</i> themselves in the ritual and symbolic trappings of death.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":7262,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","user":"Amakawa Yuuto","date":". 09-23-2015, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T13:19:12-07:00","id":675663,"title":"","content":"Oh well then totally an Army of Skeletons count. Thing is if somebody wipes out that army (Lets say a particularly determined Zenith or Scourge), the Abyssal would lose the various bonuses related to the trappings of death.<br /> <br /> This also means that stripping or otherwise destroying the clothes of an Abyssal is a pretty solid tactic in a fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T13:31:05-07:00","id":675674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=675663#post675663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh well then totally an Army of Skeletons count. Thing is if somebody wipes out that army (Lets say a particularly determined Zenith or Scourge), the Abyssal would lose the various bonuses related to the trappings of death.<br /> <br /> This also means that stripping or otherwise destroying the clothes of an Abyssal is a pretty solid tactic in a fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>oh dear... anyone yelling that as advice will probably end up in the out of context thread <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" bo