th.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T09:07:14-07:00","id":680068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=675082#post675082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's one thing I'd like to hear if anyone else does.<br /> <br /> Do anyone give their deathknights a look fitting the &quot;Theme&quot; of their deathlord (custom and canon)?<br /> for example, the deathlord known as &quot;the madman of the arena&quot; a warrior and combatant through and through.<br /> This guy is more or less a combat glutton (he became a deathlord because the neverborn promised him the greatest battle of his (un)life if he joined them).<br /> so as a theme since his base of operations is a Colosseum looking arena, I designed his deathknights to have a gladiatorial look about them (oh and he only uses dusk castes and despise archery type weapons).<br /> Have anyone else done that?</div> </div> </div> </div> That's sort of a good idea, but I just used the Scavenger Lands canon Deathlords, and honestly their theme is &quot;black and skulls&quot; so the deathlords look pretty generic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amakawa Yuuto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone considered animals?</div> </div> </div> </div> In the game I run, the one rogue Abyssal* who has appeared a lot as a friend (or, originally, &quot;friend) of the party was a Day Caste called Murder of Crows. She wore a big cloak made of crow feathers as her trappings of death, since of course crows are associated with battlefields and corpses.<br /> <br /> *Originally, she worked for MoW but pretended to be rogue. Later she joined an anti-Neverborn Sidereal/Deathlord conspiracy to try to seal off the Underworld from Creation forever, but the PCs sabotaged the plan because it had too much collateral damage.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T01:35:02-07:00","id":680760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/667904-lets-design-abyssals-sigs?p=680068#post680068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's sort of a good idea, but I just used the Scavenger Lands canon Deathlords, and honestly their theme is &quot;black and skulls&quot; so the deathlords look pretty generic.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the game I run, the one rogue Abyssal* who has appeared a lot as a friend (or, originally, &quot;friend) of the party was a Day Caste called Murder of Crows. She wore a big cloak made of crow feathers as her trappings of death, since of course crows are associated with battlefields and corpses.<br /> <br /> *Originally, she worked for MoW but pretended to be rogue. Later she joined an anti-Neverborn Sidereal/Deathlord conspiracy to try to seal off the Underworld from Creation forever, but the PCs sabotaged the plan because it had too much collateral damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>actually even the canon ones have a few themes to them that one can use now and then. We should actually try and find them all out now that i think of it.<br /> Examples.<br /> <br /> The dowager will ALWAYS have her deathknights be children. My theory is that she was a very motherly character as a solar, possibly a genesis master that saw all her genesis creations as her children and witnessed their deaths in dragon blooded death camps during and after the usurpation. Possibly making that the thing that &quot;broke&quot; her and caused her to join in with the neverborn.<br /> <br /> The walker refuses to believe that his deathknights can be anything else than their &quot;stereotypical&quot; role.<br /> <br /> The lion would probably have most of his deathknights dressed up so it clearly says who it is they represent, he has to much of an ego to let any of his death knights (except possibly day castes) do anything noticeable without making sure that everyone knows who it was that trained and armed said deathknight.<br /> <br /> Princess at the moment would make sure that her deathknight(s) would resemble the lions as much as possible just to make sure he doesn't suspect anything (or worse get's jealous).<br /> <br /> The bishops obsession with ancestor cults or rather his own death cult would most likely result in most of his deathknights being dressed as death priests, &quot;holy&quot; warriors or death acolytes.<br /> <br /> eye and seven despairs would probably not give many craps about what his deathknights wear as long as he can torment them.<br /> <br /> the mask I'm not sure about what his theme would be, possibly having them all give of a kind of &quot;nobility&quot; feel just to make it so he can look at his deathknights then look at someone else's and grin with the idea that his deathknights are superior to the &quot;rabble&quot; the others have.<br /> <br /> Bodhisattva. Naval theme, naval theme all the way. Be it the feel of a pirate or a admiral both of them work for the silver prince (possibly with the moonshadows being dressed to look as welcoming and friendly as possible just to make sure that ambassadors won't have anything beyond the ancestor worshiping to report).<br /> <br /> The lover hmm this one is a bit tricky, possibly a sort of macabre royal court feeling to it? Not completely sure.<br /> <br /> now to custom ones, here i can go wild.<br /> <br /> The Madman of the Arena. Like I described earlier, the madman is a &quot;battle glutton&quot; (he is a kind of deathlord version of kenpachi zaraki when it comes to mentality).<br /> When I use him he is the STRONGEST of the deathlords when it comes to personal combat prowess (the lion still has the largest army and is a better tactician and general by far).<br /> he is waiting for the greatest battle of his (un)life and in the meanwhile he fights armies of powerful war ghosts inside his arena (one where ghosts cannot be destroyed inside, constructed by the other deathlords just to make sure that the madman always had something to fight so he wouldn't get bored and go on a warpath).<br /> his deathknights are all dusk castes whom have a gladiatorial look and feel about them.<br /> <br /> The Reaper of the Mortal Harvest. In life he was known as one of the greatest doctors in creation, possibly THE greatest doctor of the first age.<br /> A genius in the arts of medicine and genesis crafting he uses these skills to create monstrous warriors combining different crafting skills, a lot of combat drugs and poisons.<br /> he is not one for conquest or domination, &quot;he is a man of science&quot; (to quote him) as such his base of operations is a garden of screaming nightmares.<br /> His deathknights are all monstrous abominations, results of his experiments, usually wrapped in bandages or covered in scars. (he cannot keep himself from experimenting on everything that's available to him, one of the reasons why he is the deathlord with the most rouge deathknights).<br /> <br /> The Craftsman of Genocide. He is a master craftsman, he can be very motivated if someone questions his skill (whenever anyone would go &quot;oh but maybe it's beyond your skill&quot; he would craft whatever it was they talked about just to prove them wrong).<br /> He is a craftsman first and foremost, he has no interest in conquest, all he does is to craft and invent artifacts.<br /> his deathknights are all either craftsmen like himself and/or incredibly well armed and armored (the craftsman has so many things crafted that he refuses to let any of his servants walk around without being properly equipped).<br /> <br /> The Soulless Watcher in the Dark. This guy is a mystery even to his own death knights, he is cloaked in shadow the only defining feature is his one glowing eye.<br /> He posses great knowledge and is loyal beyond reason to the neverborn. He has some sort of plan and when he speaks it is wise to listen, for those that refuse often find themselves in peril at the hands of the neverborn. His full power is unknown but he is feared and respected despite being the deathlords with one of the smallest domains and army's (he has about 100 nephwracks backed up by about a dozen hekatonkhires of varying power).<br /> his deathknights are all necromancers and posses vast knowledge of the occult. They are usually either masked or wear hoods that cover their faces in darkness. (the watcher is the deathlord with the least rouge deathknights, the ones that have dared have only ever needed to be punished once before they see the error of their way... or die).<br /> <br /> I hope i made some sense <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T04:42:04-07:00","id":685473,"title":"","content":"I decided to make yet another day caste so here you all go.<br /> say hello to &quot;Murder so Foul&quot; (not my best name)<br /> A day caste loyal to my custom deathlord known as &quot;the Soulless Watcher in the Dark&quot;.<br /> A practitioner of the custom (aka does not even exist) martial arts style known as the &quot;Iron Chain Tyrant&quot; style, last seen used in the final battle of the primordial war.<br /> link is in the first post.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margi